  \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"长PFS（>6个月） vs. 短PFS（≤6个月）\",\n          \"finding\": \"β-多样性存在显著差异。短PFS患者中厚壁菌门（Firmicutes）和放线菌门（Actinobacteria）丰度显著增加，F/B比率升高。长PFS患者中*Alistipes shahii*、*Alistipes finegoldii*和*Barnesiella visceriola*丰度较高；短PFS患者中*Streptococcus salivarius*、*S. vestibularis*和*Bifidobacterium breve*丰度较高。长PFS患者的菌群网络连接更紧密，具有更高的中心性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdf77d78260ae78820b64685\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"PD-L1低表达 vs. PD-L1高表达\",\n          \"finding\": \"β-多样性无显著差异。PD-L1低表达患者中广古菌门（Euryarchaeota）丰度显著更高。代谢通路方面，核苷酸降解、氨基酸合成和发酵通路在PD-L1低表达患者中更丰富。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0d94b1d03cfcafbfcf412a96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"化疗预处理（CHT-treated） vs. 一线未化疗（CHT-naive）\",\n          \"finding\": \"β-多样性存在显著差异。CHT预处理改变了菌群组成，但未将其推向特定的“短PFS”或“长PFS”表型。CHT-naive患者中糖酵解通路更丰富，而CHT-treated患者中氨基酸降解和碳水化合物合成通路更丰富。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e1c30f0af452acce36c85fc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机器学习预测效能\",\n          \"finding\": \"基于分类学特征（物种）的随机森林模型预测PFS的AUC为0.74；基于代谢通路的模型预测PD-L1表达的AUC为0.87。表明分类学特征更适合预测生存结局，而代谢通路更适合预测PD-L1表型。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::557f31a3e3355e0857469ce5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b9db5e9fba19073e07da37a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管抗PD-1免疫治疗在部分NSCLC患者中有效，但总体响应率较低且个体差异大。现有的PD-L1生物标志物存在局限性（如超过50%的高表达患者不响应）。因此，亟需发现能够更准确预测免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的创新性生物标志物，特别是探究肠道微生物组是否以及如何影响ICI疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf381632e4e9954b4da9150d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为62名接受抗PD-1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（发现队列），以及60名来自同一机构、接受相同治疗指南的验证队列患者。研究情境聚焦于高加索人群，分析基线粪便样本中的肠道微生物组特征，并评估其与无进展生存期（PFS）、PD-L1表达状态、化疗预处理历史及药物使用（抗生素、抗酸药、类固醇）的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43c8bd2245d1dd21101634ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物组作为预测NSCLC患者抗PD-1免疫治疗疗效的新型生物标志物的潜力。作者利用鸟枪法宏基因组测序技术，对发现队列和验证队列患者的肠道菌群进行深度分析。研究首先比较了不同临床分组间的α-多样性和β-多样性差异，随后通过单变量和多变量统计模型（Lasso回归、Cox比例风险回归）筛选与PFS相关的特异性细菌分类群和代谢通路。最后，采用随机森林机器学习算法评估分类学特征和代谢通路在预测PFS和PD-L1表达中的效能。研究确认了特定菌属/种与PFS的关联，并揭示了微生物群落网络结构在治疗反应者与非反应者间的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f4dbf3bd1ff2fc87e04d5633\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限NSCLC患者，高加索人群。PFS定义为>6个月为长，≤6个月为短。未涉及总生存期（OS）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的细菌分类群（物种水平）与ICI疗效（PFS）的关联证据。发现*Alistipes shahii*和*A. finegoldii*丰度高与长PFS相关，而*Streptococcus salivarius*、*S. vestibularis*和*B. breve*丰度高与短PFS相关。这些发现在独立验证队列中得到确认。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::feeef6f1df4ea05728330825\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"基于随机森林模型，可能存在过拟合风险，尽管使用了交叉验证。代谢通路分析样本量较小（n=37）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组特征预测效能的量化数据。分类学特征预测PFS的AUC为0.74，代谢通路预测PD-L1的AUC为0.87。同时指出α-多样性在此场景下无预测价值。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a3a5b9914305654656477c50\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅为相关性观察，未通过干预实验验证网络结构变化是否导致疗效改变。机制解释尚属推测。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了菌群网络结构可能与疗效相关的假设。长PFS患者表现出更密集的菌群网络和更高的节点中心性，暗示有益菌之间的协同互作可能增强抗肿瘤免疫。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dca49d80e01fef93b6041699\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"代谢通路数据仅来自子集。F/B比率的具体生物学机制未在本研究中深入阐明。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"分析了代谢通路（如氨基酸合成、发酵）与PD-L1表达的联系，以及厚壁菌/拟杆菌比率（F/B ratio）与短PFS的联系。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35103c949497a976bb9740b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"观察性研究，混杂因素较多。化疗方案多样，未统一标准化。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"评估了化疗预处理对肠道菌群的影响。发现化疗确实改变了菌群组成（β-多样性差异），但这种改变并未将菌群推向特定的“不良预后”表型，且化疗预处理患者中仍保留了与PFS相关的特异性菌群差异。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d728198fecb8864ce25b1c18\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"引言中提到的“分子模拟”假说（微生物抗原与肿瘤新抗原相似，激活T细胞）以及“肠-肺轴”概念。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5098926836554035c3b06b7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论部分指出本研究与东亚人群研究（Jin et al., Zhang et al.）结果的差异，归因于种族背景、测序方法（16S vs 宏基因组）和参考数据库的不同。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f539b66ea1f6e028c87c0c12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究了抗生素、抗酸药（PPI）和类固醇使用对菌群的影响。发现抗酸药使用与短PFS相关菌属（链球菌）增加有关，而抗生素使用未直接关联短PFS菌属增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24419f7508af418e94b98eeb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为观察性横断面研究，发现的菌群与PFS关联仅为统计学相关，不能直接推断因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70e5af635ac8a33a9883b412\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本主要来自高加索人群，结论外推至其他种族（如亚洲、非洲）时需考虑微生物组地域差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13e15e1ea0c2a87317c8c1e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"PFS的定义（6个月阈值）可能影响结果的解释，且未报告总生存期（OS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db4a1a595b125fa5470e038e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"代谢通路分析仅在部分患者中进行，可能不代表整体队列的功能特征。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7c19a38017d41f95e77105d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机器学习模型的预测性能（AUC 0.74）属于中等水平，尚未达到临床常规应用的极高精度标准。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ff1bcc625ac6b83f10feac7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-e07b4c340a667bb2f261\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"missing\": [\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0001_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0001_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0002_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0002_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0003_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0003_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0004_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0004_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0005_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0005_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0006_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0006_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0007_OC.jpg\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_F0007_OC.gif\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_SM7626.docx\",\n                \"KONI_A_2204746_SM7626.docx\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"graphic_members_unmatched\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\n              \"status\": \"unparsed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5e5e3399117dd84e4073c318\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b67c869eee5a32d72d756c1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::905a16b1317dae09553557fb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4fc1b23aa9738aec8d869909\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"纵向队列研究设计。收集III期黑色素瘤患者在联合ICI治疗前（基线）和治疗后第6周的配对粪便样本（n=126）和外周血PBMC样本（n=71）。使用16S rRNA基因测序分析肠道微生物组成，使用质谱流式细胞术全面 profiling 循环免疫细胞亚群。比较基线与第6周的微生物和免疫指标变化，并分析其与临床应答状态及irAEs严重程度的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ddc7133862b1e98dee7bbcc4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向证据，表明肠道微生物组（特别是拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与ICI治疗期间的免疫细胞动态（特别是Tregs）及临床结局（应答和irAEs）存在关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正）、微生物功能推断细节、以及是否控制了其他混杂因素（如抗生素使用、饮食等）。此外，作为会议摘要，缺乏完整的实验细节和长期随访数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ced063ef4d895bb2527ef3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI治疗前后对比\",\n          \"finding\": \"治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞（Tem）频率增加（P=0.0096）和调节性T细胞（Tregs）频率减少（P=0.0029）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::df0c22db80cc042e49db6078\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据临床应答分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"Tregs的减少主要在应答者中观察到（P=0.0016），而在非应答者中无显著变化（P=0.9515）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::155a4a53fa9c96215b2c32fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"根据irAEs严重程度分类\",\n          \"finding\": \"发生严重irAEs的患者在第6周时Tregs显著缺乏（P=0.0293），相比无或轻度毒性患者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4dd917c890edeb09e25c7941\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与免疫变化的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"在循环Tregs减少的患者中，Tregs减少的程度与基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）相对丰度呈正相关（P<0.0001）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43564e4cabb74c63d54ecf12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线微生物与临床结局的关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的基线拟杆菌属丰度与更严重的irAEs发展（P=0.0472）及第6周前更高的类固醇使用率（P=0.0345）相关。相反，较高的瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）丰度具有保护作用，且瘤胃球菌科主导的微生物组患者中应答者比例更高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b30b98ec45be93bfcf01d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b52da9c89aaeaaa5b0749b6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效，但具体机制不明。本研究试图解决：肠道微生物如何与免疫系统相互作用以影响ICI的成功或irAEs的发生？特别是特定细菌类群（如拟杆菌属和瘤胃球菌科）与免疫细胞亚群变化及临床结局之间的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15613d5b09de0b9d50378597\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"III期黑色素瘤患者，接受新辅助联合抗PD-1/抗CTLA-4免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗；涉及澳大利亚和荷兰队列（n=126），其中71名患者有匹配的PBMC数据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e128a47c0a17f95654887c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组与免疫系统在ICI治疗中的纵向动态关系及其对疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。通过对126名患者的基线和第6周粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序，并对71名患者的外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）进行质谱流式细胞术分析，研究发现ICI治疗导致循环中CD8+效应记忆T细胞增加和调节性T细胞（Tregs）减少。Tregs的减少主要见于应答者，但在发生严重irAEs的患者中也观察到显著缺乏。基线拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）丰度与Tregs减少程度及严重irAEs风险正相关，而瘤胃球菌科（Ruminococcaceae）高丰度则具有保护作用并关联更好的应答。结论指出肠道微生物组可能通过影响免疫平衡的“临界点”来塑造ICI的治疗结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46fff116fb877592fe07c91f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅针对III期黑色素瘤患者，且为新辅助联合ICI治疗情境；不能直接外推至其他肿瘤类型或单药ICI治疗。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌类群（拟杆菌属、瘤胃球菌科）与ICI疗效（客观缓解）及毒性（irAEs严重程度）的具体关联方向和数据支持。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ba5a4a521ab5b76c9cdd393\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察性关联提出的假设性机制（'suggests that...'），并非经过功能验证的因果机制；需结合其他研究确认其普遍性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制线索：肠道微生物组可能通过影响基线免疫稳态（特别是Tregs的水平）来设定免疫反应的‘阈值’或‘临界点’，从而影响抗肿瘤免疫和irAEs的发生。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bed1c5a92a1c909e5a7e55ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"摘要中提到‘how gut microbes interact with the immune system... remains unclear’，反映了该领域的知识空白和研究动机。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5fb91d23ecba19c99dc65b1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"拟杆菌属既与Treg减少（通常关联疗效）相关，又与严重irAEs相关；而瘤胃球菌科则显示保护性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::561b8cc96f7980e0b68fb9a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为会议摘要，详细的方法学细节（如测序深度、生物信息学流程、流式抗体面板、统计分析模型）未在摘要中提供，需谨慎引用具体数值和方法论细节。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e79b3405bb023182accfa755\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象仅限于III期黑色素瘤患者，且接受的是新辅助联合ICI治疗，结果可能不适用于晚期转移性黑色素瘤或其他实体瘤的单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fee2de282937a619aa2bdca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关联不等于因果：观察到的微生物与免疫细胞及临床结局的关联可能是由其他未测量的混杂因素驱动的，或反映的是反向因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7929958b24e5e4211328f19b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"‘拟杆菌属’是一个属水平的分类单元，其内部物种可能存在功能差异，摘要未提供更精细的分类或功能信息。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e1908b8bbd498777e918ecb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0098\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::abeae3f5437f046402745e3d\",\n          \"snapshot::6bd724179a28fdc49a979613\",\n          \"snapshot::da0f21f85aefb292e922131e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15880bc0c9b27ea149b5f481\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69a5c41c3468c7220ec3c645\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85fe10bf66a0ea72d4898c74\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性观察性试点研究。纳入标准：确诊为IIIA-IV期NSCLC并接受pembrolizumab（抗PD-1抗体）治疗的患者。数据采集：在治疗前获取基线粪便样本，在第一周期治疗后3周内获取第二次粪便样本。分析方法：使用QIIME v1.9.1进行16S rRNA序列分析，计算Alpha多样性（Observed, Chao1, Shannon, Simpson）和Beta多样性（Bray-Curtis dissimilarity + PERMANOVA）。使用DESeq2检测属水平上的差异丰度菌种。临床评估：基于iRECIST标准在第12周判定响应状态（CR/PR vs SD/PD）。统计比较：对比响应者与非响应者在治疗前后微生物组变化的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55647bb83a139b9ad1f5a1fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了小规模前瞻性数据，表明NSCLC患者在接受抗PD-1治疗期间，肠道微生物组的动态变化（而非仅基线状态）与临床响应相关。发现响应者伴随更大的微生物组多样性波动，并鉴定了特定的菌属变化模式（如响应者中Clostridium sensu stricto 1增加，无响应者中Akkermansia减少）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量极小（N=5），仅为试点研究，不足以得出确切的因果结论或普适性规律。仅收集了一个时间点的治疗后样本，无法描绘完整的纵向轨迹。未包含所有患者（特别是无响应者）的外周血CX3CR1+ CD8+ T细胞数据，限制了微生物组与系统性免疫反应的相关性分析。化疗可能干扰微生物组，但其独立影响在本研究中未完全剥离。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c7b0afc6f541c9bb294a0bd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基线阶段，3名响应者与2名无响应者之间\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物组的整体Alpha多样性（包括Observed, Chao1, Shannon, Simpson指数）无显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c233e41e0f6c2e57947aec0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"治疗期间，比较响应者与无响应者的微生物组变化幅度\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者表现出显著的治疗前后微生物组多样性变化（R2: 0.146, P = 0.0274），而无响应者变化较小。整体而言，治疗时间点对微生物组组成的解释力较弱（P = 0.26），个体效应较强。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c110c5934d43437de2c0d2ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"响应者（Responders）治疗后的特定菌属变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"Odoribacter, Gordonibacter, Candidatus Stoquefichus, Escheria-Shigella, 和 Collinsella 的丰度显著下降；Clostridium sensu stricto 1 的丰度显著增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6419dd7088c2e53b13242b6f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"无响应者（Non-responders）治疗后的特定菌属变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"Prevotella, Porphyromonas, Streptococcus, 和 Escheria-Shigella 的丰度显著增加；Akkermansia 的丰度显著下降。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ea9986a3cf5236e55a897e3f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::abc522398739e5d4c58fea4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"主要问题：目前缺乏有效的非侵入性生物标志物来早期识别对PD-1/PD-L1阻断疗法有反应的NSCLC患者，且基线微生物组与疗效的关系尚不明确。具体动机：尽管已知抗生素使用影响ICI疗效，但治疗过程中肠道微生物组的组成变化及其与疗效的具体关系仍不清楚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2d15979eaa156c5f0e78cb3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受抗PD-1免疫治疗（单药或联合化疗）的III期至IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者。研究情境为Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center的前瞻性队列，样本量为5名患者（3名响应者，2名无响应者）。范围聚焦于治疗前及早期治疗期间粪便样本中肠道微生物组的动态变化及其与临床疗效的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38d2935668ccaa759a6b6432\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物组在治疗过程中的动态变化是否能作为预测非小细胞肺癌患者对PD-1抑制剂反应的非侵入性生物标志物。鉴于基线微生物组特征和肿瘤组织PD-L1表达的预测价值有限，作者分析了5名患者的配对粪便样本，通过16S rRNA测序比较响应者与无响应者在治疗前后的微生物多样性及组成差异。研究发现，虽然基线α多样性在两组间无显著差异，但响应者在治疗期间的微生物多样性发生了显著改变，而无响应者则相对稳定或呈现不同的菌群演变模式。这表明治疗期间的微生物组波动可能与免疫治疗的疗效相关。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60bb2b4a9aa9df9db01788b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限NSCLC人群，样本量小（N=5），且混合了单药与联合化疗方案，结果的外推需谨慎。不能证明因果关系，仅为关联观察。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的临床观察证据：在NSCLC患者中，治疗期间肠道微生物组的显著变化（波动）与抗PD-1治疗的响应正相关，而稳定的或特定菌属（如Akkermansia减少）的变化与无响应相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e83c2e1bd28e65ccf7087396\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是相关性发现，未提供直接的机制验证（如代谢产物分析或动物模型验证）。所给材料未交代这些菌属变化的具体分子机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提示了潜在的机制线索：响应者中Clostridium sensu stricto 1的增加和无响应者中Akkermansia的减少可能与免疫激活或抑制有关。同时指出Escheria-Shigella在无响应者中的增加与既往文献一致。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab5db6ff6e6bd9baf462ffc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文引言讨论了基线微生物组、抗生素使用、粪菌移植（FMT）与ICI疗效的关系，以及当前基线生物标志物（如PD-L1）的局限性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7d78b42fa14a1be3044aa718\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用了16S rRNA测序（V3-V4区）和标准的生物信息学流程（QIIME, DESeq2）来分析配对样本。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bd3e81cd7e640495cb12068\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量极小（N=5），结果可能存在过拟合或偶然性，不能代表总体人群。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246effc5bffc4f5957f9d1d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究纳入了联合化疗患者，化疗本身对微生物组的影响未被单独控制，可能导致混杂。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cbe5d95acd9ad45b5d33eee2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"仅有一个治疗时间点样本，无法区分短期波动与长期趋势。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b5f55cb4a345f60d7fb9eb6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“潜在用途”需结合其他更大规模研究综合评估，不可单独视为确证证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a6c058a106fbb14db28ef44\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0134\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c668512a6c9823161aab5aff\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2e6d4dfc0cdc627820931355\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c68801c53064238d6315c89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4cbcd1bdd69fde55c51229cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 纵向数据采集：对92名接受pembrolizumab治疗的晚期NSCLC患者进行串行样本采集。2. 多组学分析：对患者样本进行肠道微生物组测序、RNA-seq和WES分析。3. 对照比较：将患者微生物数据与92名健康对照进行比较，分析免疫治疗期间的微生物特征变化。4. 队列整合与验证：结合内部队列与728例公开ICI治疗队列数据，开发用于分类ICI反应的评分。5. 评分优化：基于响应者与非响应者相关微生物标记物的比率构建跨人群评分，并与TMB联合评估其分层能力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9234bfeff0816e566ab0c7f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了纵向多组学证据，明确了特定菌群（Faecalibacterium vs Lactobacillus/Escherichia）与NSCLC患者ICI疗效的关联，并揭示了微生物失调随治疗和进展的动态轨迹。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的统计模型细节、多组学数据整合的具体算法、以及TMB联合评分在不同亚组中的具体性能指标（如AUC值）。此外，相关性不等于因果性，饮食和抗生素的影响需进一步控制混杂因素验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f5f3ff45c44d58bc524af1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在92名NSCLC患者队列中，根据RECIST标准定义的反应者（CR/PR或SD≥6个月）与非反应者对比\",\n          \"finding\": \"反应者富集Faecalibacterium属，非反应者富集Lactobacillus和Escherichia属；这些菌群的丰度与膳食纤维摄入和抗生素使用存在特定关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f962de69aff3170c50d46d9f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"纵向观察治疗期间及疾病进展时的微生物失调动态\",\n          \"finding\": \"在治疗后，仅反应者的微生物特征与健康队列的差异性降低；而在疾病进展时，无论反应者还是非反应者，其与正常队列的差异性均增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dbab987f2615c8ecf70dc648\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"利用内部队列和728例公共ICI队列数据开发的跨人群评分\",\n          \"finding\": \"该评分基于响应者/非响应者相关微生物标记物比率，与反映肠道微生物健康状态的指数呈显著正相关；当与肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）结合时，提高了ICI疗效的分层准确性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d75c5834eaf3870ae01a1445\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f891faea0d8fe7e53741a5ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组与ICI反应有关，但缺乏纵向多组学研究来明确具体因素及其动态变化机制。本研究旨在识别导致治疗反应差异的具体微生物和宿主因素，并开发一种能够跨人群验证的疗效预测评分。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9fc32fab0a091de0eb039d21\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）治疗的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者。研究情境包括内部队列（92名患者，进行纵向多组学分析）、健康对照队列（92人）以及外部公共ICI治疗队列（728人）。范围涵盖肠道微生物组、宿主转录组（RNA-seq）和全外显子组测序（WES），旨在识别影响免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的因素。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::be7f277a94f66204fd567864\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对肠道微生物组与ICI疗效关联中纵向多组学数据不足的现状，对92例晚期NSCLC患者进行了纵向采样和多组学分析。通过比较患者与健康人的微生物特征，并利用内部队列及728例公共数据开发并验证了一个分类评分系统。研究发现特定菌群丰度与治疗反应相关，观察到治疗过程中微生物失调的动态变化，并提出了一个结合肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）的跨人群评分以改善疗效分层。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c75ab0a7f525c3cdcfd56bcf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"结论基于NSCLC患者队列，虽结合了公共ICI数据，但主要发现仍局限于肺癌语境下的微生物特征；评分的有效性依赖于特定的标记物选择和健康状态指数。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的微生物分类群（Faecalibacterium, Lactobacillus, Escherichia）与ICI疗效（CR/PR/SD vs PD）的关联证据，并开发了基于这些标记物比率的跨人群评分。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::697fab1e944be79f63331cce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"摘要未提供具体的分子机制（如代谢产物、免疫细胞浸润等），仅描述了表型层面的动态变化和统计学关联；无法直接解释因果机制，仅能作为机制研究的背景或假设生成依据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了微生物失调的动态变化模式：反应者治疗后向健康状态回归，而进展期所有患者均出现恶化。同时指出微生物特征与TMB具有互补性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26c8e9ef23383e9bd70bc9a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究发现特定菌群与膳食纤维摄入和抗生素使用有关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91f6c9b443b00edda18f6269\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"微生物评分与TMB结合提高了分层准确性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf589dd5bc8c56c8193ab89d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为观察性纵向研究，发现的菌群与疗效关联为相关性，不能直接推断因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::606f3a3f6e5e9b33a1fb74d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物特征的动态变化（如治疗后向健康状态回归）仅在反应者中观察到，非反应者在进展期恶化，这一模式需谨慎外推至其他肿瘤类型或治疗线数。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8420884f93801885a20acf8b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"评分系统的开发使用了公共数据，但其具体权重和阈值未在摘要中披露，使用时需注意可重复性限制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3147586d331aea68e8905ba3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所给材料未提供详细的统计显著性数值（如P值、置信区间），仅定性描述“显著正相关”。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a4238167e6163f4ef5f1f19a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_not_scholarly_body\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_plus_snippets\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f785f081b25b8053f6af6b58\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe8dbe80e1b345cf463a700c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::63d6761df76fcc28abb72d65\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::799dc90a7500725ba934e5e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"A prospective observational cohort design was used. Clinical data for 74 patients were analyzed for associations between antibiotic/probiotic use and survival outcomes (PFS, OS, ORR) using Kaplan-Meier analysis and Cox regression. For 18 patients with complete dynamic sampling, metagenomic sequencing and untargeted metabolomics were performed. Microbial alpha/beta diversity, differential taxa abundance, and dynamic trajectory types (U-shaped vs. inverted U-shaped) were analyzed. Metabolite differences between responders and non-responders were identified via UHPLC-MS, followed by correlation analysis between specific microbial taxa and metabolites.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21b032f497e11ad82f077478\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides the first multi-omics characterization of gut microbiota and metabolites in EGFR+ NSCLC patients undergoing ICI therapy, identifying distinct microbial and metabolic signatures different from those reported in EGFR- NSCLC.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Single-center study with a small sample size for omics analysis (n=18). Observational design limits causal inference. The lack of Akkermansia muciniphila as a predictor suggests population-specific or subtype-specific differences that require validation in larger cohorts.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f31eb3ef8495f0907f8d0857\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Advanced EGFR+ NSCLC patients treated with ICIs\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use (within 2 months before/after ICI initiation) was significantly associated with shorter progression-free survival (mPFS 4.8 vs. 6.7 months; HR 3.18) and overall survival. Probiotic use had no significant impact on PFS or OS.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b00cd4addabe5f051094b7ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Comparison of responders vs. non-responders based on metagenomic sequencing\",\n          \"finding\": \"No significant difference in baseline alpha or beta diversity. Responders were enriched in Bradyrhizobium guangdongense, Plantactinospora sp., Corynebacterium stationis, and Methanococcus vannielii. Non-responders were enriched in Nocardioides sp., Candidatus thioglobus sp., Burkholderia anthina, and Brachybacterium sp. Notably, known beneficial species like Akkermansia muciniphila were not found to be predictive in this cohort.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2321908271fcad576e47dcec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Dynamic changes in gut microbiota over time (Baseline -> Response -> Progression)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Two dynamic patterns were identified in the 18 longitudinally sampled patients: 'U-type' (abundance decreased at response, increased at progression, e.g., Enterococcus gallinarum) and 'Inverted U-type' (abundance increased at response, decreased at progression, e.g., Mycobacterium paragordonae).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d378659198997c365edf5df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Metabolomic profiling of responders vs. non-responders\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders showed enrichment of deoxycholic acid, glycerol, and quinolinic acid. Non-responders showed enrichment of L-citrulline. Significant correlations were observed between specific microbial taxa and these metabolites.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::399aa4789f191d531f10450c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e7e721cb1761802b4554575\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The effects of gut microbiota and metabolites on ICI responses have been well-studied in EGFR wild-type (EGFR-) NSCLC, but remain unknown in EGFR-mutated (EGFR+) NSCLC. Given that EGFR+ tumors are often immunologically cold and show limited benefit from ICIs compared to EGFR- tumors, there is a need to elucidate whether gut microbiota characteristics can predict or influence ICI efficacy in this distinct molecular subtype.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::72b8df7aef468dc5c563524b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Advanced EGFR-mutated (EGFR+) non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) after resistance to EGFR-tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs). The study focuses on the association between clinical factors (antibiotic/probiotic use), gut microbiota composition and dynamics, fecal metabolites, and immunotherapy efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e71a1eb72eede5f1828bbca1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This prospective cohort study investigated the impact of gut microbiota and metabolites on the efficacy of ICIs in a specific subgroup of NSCLC patients with EGFR mutations. The research enrolled 74 advanced EGFR+ NSCLC patients and collected detailed clinical data regarding antibiotic and probiotic usage. Fecal samples were dynamically collected from 18 patients at four time points: baseline, early on-treatment, response, and progression. Metagenomic next-generation sequencing and ultra-high-performance liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry (UHPLC-MS) were employed to analyze microbial composition and metabolic profiles. The study aimed to identify biomarkers and mechanisms linking the gut environment to ICI outcomes in this population, which is often considered immunologically 'cold'.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ccbb8d260cff2b9ce6c84e79\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Limited to EGFR+ NSCLC; does not establish causality for probiotic neutrality.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies that antibiotic use significantly worsens PFS in EGFR+ NSCLC patients on ICIs, while probiotics have no effect. This contrasts with some studies in other cancers or EGFR- NSCLC where probiotics might show benefit, highlighting the complexity of microbiome interventions.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e1e88637ee445522384bfa4e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Based on a small omics cohort (n=18); requires validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discovers specific microbial taxa associated with response in EGFR+ NSCLC (Bradyrhizobium guangdongense, etc.) that differ from the canonical markers (e.g., Akkermansia) found in EGFR- NSCLC.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b3702a3197e89eed1f4c5e8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Correlational only; in vivo/in vitro validation is needed as stated by authors.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Links specific metabolites (deoxycholic acid, glycerol, quinolinic acid in responders; L-citrulline in non-responders) to microbial taxa and clinical response. Suggests metabolic pathways like tryptophan metabolism and lipolysis regulation as potential mediators.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08db0dba8af6563011c2fd5f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion notes that EGFR+ tumors are immunologically cold and that baseline diversity did not differ between responders/non-responders, unlike in some EGFR- studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d63c43f8d3cba44a960ee6a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Identification of 'U-type' and 'Inverted U-type' dynamic trajectories of microbial abundance relative to treatment response and progression.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2581070271d137c95ba7e99f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Findings are specific to EGFR-mutated NSCLC; results cannot be directly extrapolated to EGFR-wild type or other solid tumors without caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0aec56d0c003ddcdfad97f7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The omics analysis is based on a small subset (18 patients) of the total cohort (74 patients); statistical power for microbial/metabolic associations is limited.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b64e2f1e48a78dcdb499a56f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The study is observational; associations between antibiotics/microbiota and outcomes do not prove causation.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf640c1bebb2844ced09d6be\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Probiotic neutrality should not be interpreted as proof of ineffectiveness in all contexts, but rather as an observation in this specific cohort with potentially varying probiotic formulations/durations.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ed527d6672ea83dc3ced6b92\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::428346e86e6d583a8d61c3e7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43292a8e25697a7a2b821c6a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05c6ea6e669a12d87d90425b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31cba66826bdd392741dbc24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性观察性队列研究。收集27例黑色素瘤患者治疗前粪便样本，分别进行16S rRNA基因测序（V4区）和鸟枪法宏基因组测序。其中17例样本因RNA质量合格进一步进行宏转录组测序。统计分析方面，使用Cox比例风险模型调整协变量（年龄、性别、BMI、分期等），评估α多样性、β多样性聚类及特定分类单元/功能通路与PFS的关联。采用500次×10折交叉验证的弹性网络惩罚Cox回归筛选显著相关的特征。宏转录组部分，计算基因家族、反应和通路的相对表达量，并与宏基因组丰度进行Spearman相关性分析，以确认功能的转录活性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee7c7106cfc2e786d4d2e4a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了在人类黑色素瘤患者中，肠道微生物组成、特定物种及宏基因组功能通路（含转录表达）与免疫治疗无进展生存期关联的证据；首次在同一研究中整合宏基因组与宏转录组数据以关联临床预后。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（n=27，宏转录组n=17）；未能单独分析辅助治疗与转移性患者亚组，也未能按免疫治疗类型（单药vs联合）分层分析；宏转录组分析因样本量限制统计效力不足；结果可能存在队列特异性，需更大规模研究验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24acf74201156137d9b43346\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"27例黑色素瘤患者，调整协变量后\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的微生物群落丰富度（16S s-OTU数和鸟枪法子物种数）与较长的无进展生存期（PFS）显著相关（p < 0.05）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0b1a04089a4113806fc84ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于JSD距离的Ward层次聚类，区分高、中、低风险组\",\n          \"finding\": \"低风险组（富集F. prausnitzii等）相比高风险组（富集Bacteroides spp.）在任何随访时间点具有99%更低的进展风险（HR=0.01, p=0.002）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec8e3d930bc2c3e508c94a15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"500×10折交叉验证弹性网络Cox回归筛选\",\n          \"finding\": \"与较短PFS相关的物种包括：Bacteroides ovatus, Bacteroides dorei, Bacteroides massiliensis, Ruminococcus gnavus, Blautia producta；与较长PFS相关的物种包括：Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Coprococcus eutactus, Prevotella stercorea, Streptococcus sanguinis, Streptococcus anginosus, Lachnospiraceae bacterium 3 1 46FAA。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8be25514637782d7f88627e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"宏基因组与宏转录组联合分析（n=17子集）\",\n          \"finding\": \"识别出与PFS相关且具有显著转录表达的宏基因组通路：风险相关通路包括L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸生物合成、B族维生素（泛酸、吡哆醛-5-磷酸、黄素、叶酸前体）生物合成；保护相关通路包括L-异亮氨酸生物合成。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e353b4848cda9d7ba50ea4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0aeee4fa349ad6804e7718af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"既往关于肠道微生物影响免疫治疗的研究结果不一致，且多数仅关注物种丰度而未考虑功能表达，也未充分利用时间-事件数据（常二分化患者为响应者/非响应者）。本研究试图通过整合16S、宏基因组和宏转录组数据，更精确地鉴定与无进展生存期相关的特定微生物类群和功能通路，并探索其潜在的机制联系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29a4f46df8425be012292ee7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"27例接受免疫治疗（抗PD-1或抗CTLA-4）的转移性或辅助性黑色素瘤患者；研究基于治疗前粪便样本，采用16S rRNA基因测序、鸟枪法宏基因组测序及子集（n=17）的宏转录组测序；主要终点为无进展生存期（PFS）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a77bfdf071594bc0086aebd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探究肠道微生物群对黑色素瘤免疫治疗疗效的影响。通过对27名患者的治疗前粪便样本进行多组学分析，研究发现较高的微生物群落丰富度与较长的无进展生存期相关。基于整体微生物组成的聚类分析将患者分为高、中、低风险组，其中低风险组的疾病进展风险显著低于高风险组。在物种层面，拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）中的部分菌种（如B. ovatus, B. dorei）与较短的PFS相关，而粪杆菌属（Faecalibacterium）中的F. prausnitzii等则与较长的PFS相关。此外，研究首次结合宏转录组数据，识别出与PFS相关的宏基因组功能通路及其转录表达，包括L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸生物合成和B族维生素生物合成等风险相关通路，以及异亮氨酸生物合成等保护相关通路。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::00b11793deff66a1d919563f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限黑色素瘤患者；样本量小；未区分不同免疫药物类型的差异；关联而非因果。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组成（丰富度、聚类分组）和特定物种丰度与免疫治疗疗效（PFS）正负向关联的具体数据。证实了较高丰富度和特定保护性菌种（如F. prausnitzii）与更好预后相关，而特定风险菌种（如B. ovatus）与较差预后相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::871f50f4dcbe93707acc51ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅为推测，基于相关性分析；宏转录组样本量有限（n=17），统计效力不足；无法直接证明这些通路在体内确实导致了免疫调节；所给摘要未交代具体的代谢物浓度测量或动物实验验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了潜在的机制线索：识别出与PFS相关的宏基因组功能通路及其转录表达。具体包括：风险通路（L-鼠李糖降解、鸟苷核苷酸合成、B族维生素合成）和保护通路（L-异亮氨酸合成）。作者推测这些代谢产物可能通过影响T细胞功能或肿瘤微环境来调节疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff44063c2bde32931bb20b1a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文讨论了既往研究（Gopalakrishnan et al., Matson et al.等）在物种发现上的不一致性，并指出功能冗余可能是关键决定因素的观点。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::345c79f514e73c54a4e5a1ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用了16S、宏基因组和宏转录组的多组学整合策略，以及500×10折交叉验证的弹性网络Cox回归进行特征选择。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb725823ea2bd9cc8e0f9c70\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究仅在黑色素瘤中进行，结论不能直接外推至其他固体肿瘤，尽管综述主题包含所有固体肿瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a49e41e5085e72c62aeb151e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"宏转录组数据仅来自17名患者，因此关于转录表达与预后的关联应被视为初步探索性结果，统计效力受限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f7fc3caa6b68a944e1d98686\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者提出的机制（如代谢物影响T细胞）是基于文献引用的推测，并非本研究的直接实验证据，需在综述中明确区分观察到的关联与提出的假设。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d46959426cc7755d82f0e7f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"未区分辅助治疗与转移性患者，也未按免疫治疗类型分层，因此无法判断微生物效应是否受治疗阶段或药物类型调节。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e152719a4ba4f5b110b4a7c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0415\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7de762c194aeb4f84f1e\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3778ce1ca15de297b1179ec8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::025edc534ec6facc5918e970\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ecf117da6fb0ce8cf42daec5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ec8717ea1fb9c13cffbce1b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"前瞻性队列设计：连续纳入MD Anderson的MM患者。样本采集包括：(1) 粪便标本（全宏基因组鸟枪法测序WMS、微生物组分析及16S rRNA基因测序）；(2) 黏膜表面拭子（WMS测序）；(3) FFPE肿瘤标本（Bruker数字空间 profiling DSP）；(4) 新鲜肿瘤样本（正常和肿瘤组织的WES/WGS、RNA测序、T细胞受体测序）。分析重点在于比较不同原发部位微生物特征的异质性、肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）及突变签名，并对比ICI治疗响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的微生物组成差异及DSP免疫标记物表达水平。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a63e039ca90b3c9c6ce663cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了黏膜黑色素瘤不同原发部位（口鼻、泌尿生殖、直肠等）的特异性微生物组和基因组特征基线数据；初步揭示了ICI响应者与响应者在肠道菌群组成及肿瘤微环境免疫标记物（CD56, CD20）上的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"研究仍在进行中，仅报告了部分入组患者的初步分析结果，缺乏完整的长期随访疗效数据；样本量相对较小（n=130，其中完成微生物组测序85人）；未提供具体的因果机制验证，仅为相关性观察；摘要未交代统计分析的具体细节及多重比较校正方法。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bc1422b9fae5b64d5014930b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于截至2026年5月入组的130名患者（已测序粪便和黏膜拭子85人），按原发部位分类。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道和黏膜表面微生物组显示出广泛的样本内异质性，且微生物特征与原发部位相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fad70e7d4cee75ed5a89c85\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于WES和WGS数据分析。\",\n          \"finding\": \"肿瘤突变负荷（TMB）中位数为1.34 mut/Mb（范围0.52–14.72）。直肠和泌尿生殖道肿瘤与DNA错配修复和微卫星不稳定性相关的突变签名有关；结膜和口鼻肿瘤与紫外线暴露相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26a92b9bc963407db444dccb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"针对接受ICI治疗的患者的肠道微生物组分析。\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）之间细菌类群的存在和比例存在组成差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c9fa6ec476c115cb9276312c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"DSP分析按治疗反应分组。\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）的免疫和肿瘤区室中CD56和CD20的表达高于非响应者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef634aa1dff03d968764acf4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::891c061f6e1b35c8496600b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黏膜黑色素瘤是一种罕见亚型，对ICI反应率低。本研究试图确定肠道、黏膜和肿瘤微生物组以及可改变的风险因素如何影响ICI的响应和耐药，特别是通过解析微生物组与肿瘤微环境的相互作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::99d5bdcfbf4a118d8408c980\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黏膜黑色素瘤（MM）患者队列，涉及肠道、黏膜表面及肿瘤微环境的微生物组与宿主免疫/基因组互作；研究情境为前瞻性观察性研究，数据截至2026年5月。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::938112d9bf702269316f1024\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在阐明微生物组与肿瘤微环境相互作用如何驱动黏膜黑色素瘤对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的响应与耐药。研究在MD安德森癌症中心前瞻性纳入MM患者，收集粪便、黏膜拭子及肿瘤组织样本进行多组学分析。初步结果显示，不同原发部位的MM具有特定的微生物特征和突变谱；在接受ICI治疗的患者中，响应者与非响应者在肠道菌群组成上存在差异，且响应者肿瘤微环境中CD56和CD20表达更高。这是一项正在进行中的研究，目前提供了部分基线数据和初步关联结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3caf73fb053b6436a58289fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限黏膜黑色素瘤亚型；结果为初步相关性，尚未确立因果性或普适性；样本量有限。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了黏膜黑色素瘤患者中，ICI响应者与非响应者之间肠道微生物组组成的具体差异证据（细菌类群存在和比例的变化）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::174dac331c10482c9b499eeb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"CD56/CD20表达与微生物组之间的直接因果联系未在摘要中证实，仅为并行观察到的现象；机制解释尚不明确，需进一步实验验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提示了微生物组可能与肿瘤微环境免疫状态相关联，表现为响应者中CD56和CD20表达升高。同时指出了不同原发部位MM具有不同的突变签名（如MMR缺陷 vs UV损伤），这可能间接影响免疫原性和微生物组互作。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b2f4a369c8011c98960b26ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"不同原发部位（口鼻、泌尿生殖、直肠、结膜）MM具有独特的微生物特征和基因组突变签名（如UV暴露相关 vs MMR缺陷相关）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32396aee7cbda217c69e93a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MM整体对ICI反应率低，且本研究正在探索可改变的风险因素。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1ccc88cdddfbf0f6f604fa46\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为进行中中的前瞻性队列，数据截至2026年5月，结果仅为初步分析，不代表最终结论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7252567914c781709c40c1f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物组与ICI响应的关联仅为观察性相关性，未证明因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3414ff342a8a474b3279096c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量较小（n=130），且仅部分患者完成了微生物组测序，可能存在选择偏倚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11978337d32cb53b592725f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同原发部位的生物学差异巨大，结果不可直接外推至其他类型的黑色素瘤或实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::be82f4a21379d0105e536ace\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"CD56和CD20的高表达是响应者的特征，但其与微生物组的具体互作机制未知。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e412dc26845f73c0fdf22063\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0485\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ddae59555ff66f6d76f4f5d4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a99646db3b749ddfd25fe40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::deb5f1b5a0ec5f896f857444\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08554aa4c222491df9d38ef8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Single-arm, multicenter phase I clinical trial. Patients received bowel preparation, followed by oral administration of capsules containing stool from one of three healthy male donors. Anti-PD1 therapy (nivolumab or pembrolizumab) started at least 7 days post-FMT. Outcomes were assessed using RECIST 1.1 criteria. Survival analysis used Kaplan-Meier methods. Metagenomic sequencing was performed on stool samples to analyze taxonomic composition (MetaPhlAn) and functional gene families (HUMAnN). Post hoc subgroup analyses compared responders vs. non-responders and patients with vs. without FMT-specific toxicity (FT) based on microbial and functional profiles.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::37fd84d50ba8233eb66b5714\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides long-term survival data (median OS 52.8 months) for a small cohort of advanced melanoma patients treated with oral FMT plus anti-PD1, demonstrating high safety and promising efficacy signals compared to historical controls.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Small sample size (N=20), single-arm design without a control group, and lack of statistical power for definitive conclusions. Results are hypothesis-generating. Patient selection bias (excluded those appropriate for combination therapy).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7e3e6165a31ec1e105e75b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies potential biomarkers for response, linking FMT-specific mild toxicity and long-term survival to specific microbial taxa (e.g., SCFA producers) and functional metabolic pathways (glycan modification, SCFA biosynthesis).\",\n          \"limits\": \"Associations are derived from post hoc analyses. Causality between specific microbes/enzymes and clinical benefit is not established. The 'donor effect' could not be clearly disentangled due to the small cohort and mixed donor usage.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::024518a823f6006dd3e972f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Entire cohort (N=20), median follow-up 52.8 months\",\n          \"finding\": \"Median PFS was 29.6 months; median OS was 52.8 months. ORR was 65% (4 complete responses). Safety profile showed no increase in severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs); only grade 3 toxicities occurred.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3485959e4adbd9d7481e46dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Responders (R, N=13) vs. Non-responders (NR, N=7)\",\n          \"finding\": \"R patients had significantly longer mPFS (52.8 vs. 5.2 months, p=0.0016) and longer mOS (52.8 vs. 17.6 months, p=0.0628). R patients sustained donor-derived microbial similarity over time.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ebb834ea4cc8b7658e4ac8d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients with FMT-specific toxicity (FT, N=8) vs. Without FT (NFT, N=12)\",\n          \"finding\": \"All 8 FT patients were responders. FT patients had significantly improved mPFS (52.8 vs. 15.9 months, p=0.0364) and trend towards improved mOS (53.9 vs. 24.6 months, p=0.0610). FT was associated with enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa and glycan-modifying enzymes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dffaafcf80cafef8980d6a54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Long-term survivors (LTS) vs. Short-term survivors (STS)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LTS were enriched for commensal bacteria (Alistipes, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes involved in amino acid/SCFA biosynthesis. STS were enriched for stress-associated oxidative metabolism pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a938bbf69ccdde1dcf569c84\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::19f5ba98faa7f71a33a18835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To evaluate whether modifying the gut microbiome via oral FMT from healthy donors can improve the safety, response rate, and survival outcomes of anti-PD1 therapy in patients with advanced melanoma who are naive to advanced-stage treatment, potentially overcoming primary resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f99b8e9719b07fd9b3d34bf5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Advanced cutaneous melanoma patients (N=20), treatment-naïve for advanced disease, receiving oral fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) from healthy donors followed by single-agent anti-PD1 therapy. Multicenter phase I trial conducted in Canada.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::835431f5f287a104ceabd51e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This study reports the final survival outcomes of the MIMic phase I trial, evaluating the safety and efficacy of combining oral FMT with healthy donor stool and anti-PD1 immunotherapy as first-line treatment for advanced melanoma. The trial enrolled 20 patients who received a single dose of FMT followed by nivolumab or pembrolizumab. The primary endpoint was safety, while secondary endpoints included objective response rate (ORR), progression-free survival (PFS), and overall survival (OS). The study found that the combination was safe, with an ORR of 65%. Median PFS was 29.6 months and median OS was 52.8 months, figures reported as higher than historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) and real-world data. Post hoc analyses linked clinical responses to specific microbial engraftment patterns and functional metabolic pathways, suggesting that successful microbiome modulation may enhance ICI efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f8959cd8dd927a10f9dd3654\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Results are from a single-arm, small-sample Phase I trial. Cannot establish causal superiority over standard care due to lack of concurrent control arm. Patient population was restricted to those unsuitable for combination immunotherapy.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Reports clinical efficacy outcomes (ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 mo, mOS 52.8 mo) for FMT+anti-PD1 in advanced melanoma, showing improvements over historical RCT benchmarks for anti-PD1 alone.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da8e241ae0ffdf09b558a4ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are inferred from correlative post hoc analyses. The role of FMT-specific toxicity as a proxy for engraftment success is observational. Functional profiling relies on metagenomic prediction, which may not reflect actual protein activity or host interaction.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Links clinical response to specific microbial features: Responders and long-term survivors show enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa (Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes for glycan modification/amino acid biosynthesis. Non-responders/short-term survivors show enrichment of oxidative/stress pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d1f3aa72134d1a09a615318\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Comparison of oral capsule-based FMT (this study) vs. invasive colonoscopic FMT (referenced in intro). This study supports the feasibility and safety of oral delivery for systemic immune modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76bf45b8fc5ee9800416db98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"No increase in severe irAEs; FMT-specific toxicities were mild (Grade 1-2 GI).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb82a0f9f419547426bb1f12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Acknowledges small sample size, lack of control arm, and hypothesis-generating nature of results.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::754021e869ff2a2dba53a7aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The study population is limited to advanced cutaneous melanoma patients ineligible for combination immunotherapy; results may not generalize to other solid tumors or earlier-stage disease.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a37fb175d8428498e2cdd297\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Survival comparisons with historical RCTs are noted by authors but are confounded by patient selection biases and temporal changes in care; do not treat as definitive proof of superiority.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de45d8ce55cd7c245f96e6fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Microbial associations are correlational; causality between specific taxa/pathways and ICI response is not proven within this study design.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::faf64be5a80ca4ce1d2dbf3a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::004e7d4bb46dac64f072d7f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e055ed851f0bbe3c6e1076f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为20名晚期黑色素瘤患者；供体为3名健康男性；给药方式为口服胶囊；预处理为PEG肠道准备；无抗生素使用。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MIMic试验使用了来自三位健康男性供体的粪便进行口服FMT。所有患者均接受单一供体的粪便（每位患者对应一位供体），未混合多供体粪便。供体经过“严格的选择标准”筛选（文中引用了之前的出版物Craven et al. 2017及Routy et al. 2023中的详细标准）。FMT产品以胶囊形式给药，每剂包含35-40粒胶囊，相当于80-100克粪便。在给予FMT前一天，患者使用聚乙二醇（PEG）基肠道准备液进行预处理，且治疗期间未使用抗生素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R12\",\n                \"R13\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为FMT干预标准化中供体筛选和制备流程的具体案例，展示如何通过严格筛选和健康供体来源来保证干预的一致性和安全性，同时指出单供体使用的局限性。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MIMic试验在供体筛选和FMT制备方面采取了高度标准化的策略，旨在确保干预的安全性和微生物定植的可预测性。\\n\\n1. **供体筛选标准**：研究采用了“严格的选择标准”（stringent selection criteria）来筛选健康供体。虽然正文未列出具体排除指标的细节，但明确引用了关于代谢综合征疾病FMT供体筛选成本的研究（Craven et al., 2017, R13）以及该团队之前发表的I期试验方案（Routy et al., 2023, R12），暗示其遵循了当时临床前或早期临床试验中较为严格的卫生学、传染病及健康状况筛查流程。这种严格筛选是作为正面教材的，因为它最大限度地降低了传播病原体或引入致病微生物的风险，确保了“健康供体粪便”这一干预物的纯净度。\\n\\n2. **FMT制备与给药流程**：\\n   - **单一供源 vs 混合供源**：试验设计采用单一供体粪便（single healthy donor stool），每位患者仅接受来自三位指定男性供体中某一人的粪便。这种做法简化了批次管理，减少了不同供体间微生物组异质性带来的混杂因素，有利于评估特定微生物组合对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的反应。然而，这也可能是一个反面教材或局限性，因为缺乏多供体混合可能无法覆盖更广泛的有益菌群多样性，且文中提到“没有明显的供体效应”，说明单个供体的效果在不同患者间可能存在差异，但未深入探讨混合供体是否会更优。\\n   - **制剂形式**：将粪便制成口服胶囊（35-40粒/剂，含80-100g粪便），而非传统的灌肠或鼻胃管给药。这提高了患者的依从性，减少了侵入性操作带来的感染风险，是FMT非侵入化、标准化的重要进展。\\n   - **预处理与辅助措施**：在FMT前一日使用PEG基肠道准备液，旨在清除原有肠道内容物，为新菌群定植腾出生态位。特别值得注意的是，研究中明确禁止使用抗生素，以避免抗生素对肠道菌群的破坏干扰FMT的效果或引起耐药性问题。这种“清洁但不杀菌”的准备策略是标准化流程中的关键控制点。\\n\\n总体而言，该试验通过严格的供体准入、单一的供体来源、标准化的胶囊制剂以及特定的肠道预处理，构建了一套可重复的FMT干预流程。其成功的关键在于确保了输入菌群的健康属性和定植潜力，为后续观察微生物组变化与临床疗效的关系提供了可靠的基础。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"文中引用的供体筛选具体指标（如具体的病原体检测列表、BMI限制、饮食要求等）未在本文正文中详细列出，需参考R12和R13获取完整细节。\",\n            \"单一供体与多供体混合在长期定植稳定性和临床获益上的比较数据不足，仅观察到无显著供体效应，未深入分析为何选择单一供体而非混合供体。\",\n            \"PEG肠道准备的具体配方浓度、体积及服用时间未详细说明。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::25fa34eabb812f0508d3952a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d9a7b270e9001642aeaeb4d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::838e53ce99defdb274a4f6da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297360b98d6705da27fdef6c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3a4f29ae0327075e8a0f972\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0eee6b0fc85c1aa61c7d0f69\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法。电子数据库搜索策略包括关键词“cancer”、“immunotherapy/immune checkpoint inhibitor”和“microbiome/microbiota”。纳入标准限定为：成人（>18岁）、英文全文、同行评审期刊发表的研究。排除动物模型研究以专注于临床应用证据。对纳入的10项研究进行定性综合，按癌症类型（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）和治疗结果（疗效、irAEs、FMT干预）分类整理发现。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f0e5381ebc2cc88f3e2bff9f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次专门针对临床研究的综述，汇总了肠道微生物组作为ICIs疗效预测生物标志物和irAEs风险因子的证据，强调了FMT在逆转耐药性方面的初步临床可行性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所纳入的研究样本量普遍较小（多数n≤42），存在异质性（不同癌症类型、不同ICI药物、不同测序方法如16S rRNA与宏基因组）。观察性研究无法确立因果关系。未对纳入的非随机研究进行严格的质量偏倚风险评估。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cd1eb32400edde04370e97c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受ICIs治疗的晚期癌症患者（黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC等）\",\n          \"finding\": \"基线肠道微生物组的多样性和组成与ICIs疗效显著相关。高α-多样性通常与较长的PFS和OS相关。特定菌属富集与响应正相关（如Fecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila），而某些拟杆菌目（Bacteroidales）丰度高则与非响应相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5d7e1fba79b4eaef4b2e294\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受CTLA-4抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"低丰度的Bacteroidetes门细菌与免疫检查点抑制剂诱导的结肠炎（GI毒性）相关；相反，较高的Bacteroidetes丰度与抵抗结肠炎发生相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10fa00141f5ccb618952ade4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤患者接受来自响应者的FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"两项突破性临床试验显示，将来自免疫治疗响应者的粪菌移植给难治性患者，结合抗PD-1治疗，可使部分患者重新获得临床响应（Baruch et al. 3/10响应；Davar et al. 6/15响应），且安全性良好。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::322e6c1f1dc5e420331aed00\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e9b4c255e7f49de211bb37f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫疗法提高了部分晚期癌症患者的生存率，但仅少数患者受益且常伴随严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。目前尚缺乏基于临床证据的指导方针来利用肠道微生物组预测治疗反应或管理副作用。本研究试图厘清肠道微生物组作为预测生物标志物的潜力及其在增强疗效和减少副作用中的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da974f2fb7161247d30ad326\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床癌症患者（晚期转移性黑色素瘤、肝细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌及肾细胞癌），聚焦于免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）治疗前后的肠道微生物组特征及其与疗效和不良事件的关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39e920e15e0d4141f1858275\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述旨在评估肠道微生物组对癌症患者免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）临床结局及相关不良事件（AEs）的影响。作者检索了截至2021年3月的PubMed、Medline和ScienceDirect数据库，筛选出10项涉及成年人的临床研究。研究综合分析了基线微生物组的多样性（α/β多样性）和组成成分与ICIs疗效（无进展生存期PFS、总生存期OS）及胃肠道毒性（如结肠炎）之间的关联，并探讨了粪菌移植（FMT）在难治性患者中的潜在调节作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0539b1b2c53b3d7b72cb824c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些关联主要基于观察性研究，存在癌症类型异质性和样本量小的限制，不能直接推断因果机制。不同研究中具体差异菌种存在不一致性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了多项临床研究数据，表明基线肠道微生物组的特定组成（如Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, Bifidobacterium longum, Akkermansia muciniphila的高丰度）和较高多样性与ICIs治疗的良好临床响应（延长PFS/OS）相关。同时指出Bacteroidales的高丰度与非响应相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::080e444842a4a14c522c5a13\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅两项研究涉及此方面，且主要针对CTLA-4抑制剂，推广至其他ICI需谨慎。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了肠道微生物组与免疫治疗不良反应（特别是结肠炎）的联系。低Bacteroidetes丰度与CTLA-4诱导的结肠炎风险增加相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0fc5763ac32ca8ee7111a467\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"样本量极小，仅为概念验证性质。供体和受体间的个体差异、预处理抗生素的使用等因素可能影响结果。尚未阐明具体的分子机制或关键菌株。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"通过FMT临床试验（Baruch et al., Davar et al.）展示了从响应者向难治者移植微生物组可恢复部分患者的治疗响应，并观察到CD8+ T细胞激活增加和IL-8表达髓系细胞减少。这为微生物组介导免疫治疗效应的因果假设提供了最强的临床间接证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0151b710263ede70d23b60e6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要是相关性观察，未详细区分抗生素种类、使用时机及具体影响的菌群通路。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"指出抗生素使用（尤其是ICIs期间）与较差的PFS和OS相关，提示抗生素引起的菌群失调可能是导致免疫治疗耐药的一个因素。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::71bcf8d226c8b935ca4f2b4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出目前尚无基于临床证据的指南来利用微生物组指导免疫治疗，且既往综述多包含动物模型，导致临床应用存在差距。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::327e635fac3256de3a41f1db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到现有研究在测序方法（16S vs 宏基因组）、样本采集时间点上的异质性，以及缺乏标准化的偏倚评估工具。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::89b7ba4679aef53d9192191a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"汇总了黑色素瘤、HCC、NSCLC中不同的优势菌种（如黑色素瘤中Faecalibacterium，HCC中Akkermansia/Ruminococcaceae，NSCLC中Akkermansia/Alistipes）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7b952d0d492ff2d26e93bff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述仅纳入临床研究，排除了动物实验，因此其关于机制的解释（如T细胞激活）主要基于人类临床样本的相关性或FMT后的表型变化，而非直接的分子通路解析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b81452e6f8c2cf88f589c219\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"发现的菌群与疗效的关联多为观察性结果，存在混杂因素（如饮食、生活方式、合并用药），不能直接视为因果证据，除非有FMT等干预性研究的支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17045e9a74e743196a9ec5a9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同研究间使用的测序区域（V3-V4, V4, V4-V5）和分析方法不同，导致具体菌种鉴定可能存在偏差，比较时需考虑技术异质性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91f185a2d063fd5c2d47e7ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT研究样本量极小（n=10, n=15），结果仅代表初步安全性和可行性，不能代表普遍疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7acb9f11d1a63262fa2e4e18\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"phase_iii_rct_evidence\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\N48436b3aa73aea86f35f-f45b87be8e30256e\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\phase_iii_rct_evidence\\\\attempt-c7j_i2fn\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_2d56a11919\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The specific evidence requested—completed large-scale randomized controlled Phase III clinical trials confirming microbiome intervention (FMT) efficacy in ICI-treated solid tumors—is not present in this material. The available FMT data is limited to small-sample (n=10, n=15), early-phase studies restricted to refractory melanoma, not broad solid tumors. The authors' call for future robust RCTs and multicentre trials indicates that such Phase III evidence does not yet exist or was not captured in this review (search up to March 2021).\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study is a clinical review analyzing 10 studies (total n=467 patients) regarding the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) outcomes in solid tumors (melanoma, HCC, NSCLC, RCC). It reports that baseline microbiome diversity and composition (e.g., enrichment of Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS), while Bacteroidales abundance often correlates with non-response. Crucially for the gap, the authors highlight two FMT clinical studies (Baruch et al., n=10; Davar et al., n=15) in anti-PD-1 refractory metastatic melanoma. These studies demonstrated safety and potential efficacy (30-40% response rate) when combining FMT from responders with ICI re-challenge. However, the authors explicitly state that 'further well-designed RCTs are required to explore the causal effects' and that 'future international multicentre trials will be required to provide comprehensive and reliable data.' They note that up-to-date practice guidelines based on clinical evidence are not yet available.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5f4a3067c60d9ca5815c45e7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2694ad4ea52a0088aba17fec\",\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\",\n          \"snapshot::17ec529e254380cf6b84cb88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c0275a5e34adb0279612f6a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::eb554c2581ab757501df96e5\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55fcb0fa55f265c2bb14e723\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e98e7309914d20548e6cd26\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c752d967993b9b3b7603d723\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用前瞻性观察性队列设计。纳入标准：III/IV期NSCLC候选ICI治疗者；排除标准：其他组织学类型、合并肿瘤、自身免疫病、ECOG评分≥2、既往免疫治疗史、高剂量皮质类固醇使用或已知免疫缺陷。样本采集：基线粪便和血液样本。分析方法：1. 微生物组：16S rDNA V3/V4区测序，ASV分类，Shannon指数计算Alpha多样性，LEfSe进行Beta多样性及差异物种分析。2. 代谢物：GC-MS定量粪便SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸等）。3. 通透性：HPLC测血浆瓜氨酸，化学发光法测抗瓜氨酸抗体，ELISA测Zonulin，LAL法测内毒素。4. 临床关联：RECIST标准评估肿瘤反应，记录irAEs，Kaplan-Meier分析生存期，Pearson/Spearman相关性分析整合变量。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04c94e3ebea4e25ebe48718f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了NSCLC患者在接受ICI治疗前肠道微生物群、SCFA谱和肠道通透性基线特征的详细数据，证实了该人群肠道菌群的丰富性和屏障功能的完整性。首次报告了根据ICI反应和irAE状态分组的NSCLC患者循环内毒素水平。\",\n          \"limits\": \"未能确立任何预测性生物标志物。存在方法学局限性：缺乏肠道通透性测量的标准化程序和断点值；SCFA正常值尚未建立，阻碍跨研究比较；样本量有限（N=55）；患者接受的ICI药物种类多样（Durvalumab, Pembrolizumab等），可能引入异质性；未区分不同ICI药物对结果的影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a90cd6509aa34163240bad42\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"N=55 NSCLC患者，基线样本，多中心/单中心（Aragón）\",\n          \"finding\": \"未检测到肠道微生物组成、SCFA丰度或肠道通透性指标与ICI治疗反应（响应者vs非响应者）或irAE发生之间的统计学显著相关性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7a0d85d35ad699ecb5e5663\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"LEfSe差异分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者在Bacillota门（包括Clostridia和Monoglobus）中丰度较高，Hungatella在非响应者中较高；发生irAEs的患者Betaproteobacteria和Enterococcus丰度较高。但整体Alpha/Beta多样性无组间差异，且这些差异未转化为预测能力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c76c4cadc3a86cae5e2ded13\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFA分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"粪便中主要SCFA为乙酸(56%)、丙酸(19%)和丁酸(11%)，各组间分布无显著差异，且SCFA水平与细菌丰度或临床结局无关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ec73ffdf15f6f13395a316a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肠道通透性指标\",\n          \"finding\": \"瓜氨酸分散度高，抗瓜氨酸抗体在90%样本中不可检测，Zonulin和内毒素水平离散度低。所有通透性指标均未显示出预测价值。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7edd84f89163acdfe329e2f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ebe73d0fbe36fc556bf60bd5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"目前NSCLC患者对ICI治疗的总体响应率较低（15-20%），且缺乏可靠的预测生物标志物，同时部分患者会出现严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。既往研究提示肠道微生物可能影响ICI疗效，但具体机制和标志物尚不明确，且肠道通透性这一宿主因素常被忽视。本研究试图确定肠道微生物群、其代谢产物（SCFAs）以及肠道屏障完整性是否可作为预测ICI疗效和毒性的有效生物标志物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::20d0bd74bfeb5c2c59eb251a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，研究肠道微生物群组成、短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）丰度及肠道膜通透性作为治疗反应和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）预测生物标志物的可能性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1ffdc646d0901680e004cd87\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在识别NSCLC患者中预测ICI疗效和毒性的生物标志物，重点考察肠道微环境。研究招募了55名接受不同ICI方案（如Durvalumab, Pembrolizumab等）的III期或IV期NSCLC患者，在基线时收集粪便和血液样本。通过16S rDNA扩增测序分析肠道菌群组成，利用GC-MS测定粪便中的短链脂肪酸含量，并通过血浆检测瓜氨酸、抗瓜氨酸抗体、Zonulin和内毒素水平来评估肠道屏障通透性。统计分析包括描述性统计、生存分析（Kaplan-Meier）、相关性分析及LEfSe差异分析。结果显示，尽管患者肠道菌群丰富多样且功能均一，但未能发现任何肠道微生物组成、代谢产物或通透性指标与ICI治疗反应或irAE发生之间的显著相关性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f7b52aa894524dc65e6a393e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于NSCLC患者；基线静态测量；多种ICI药物混合分析；未解决因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了NSCLC特定亚群中肠道微生物与ICI疗效关系的实证数据：未发现显著关联。具体显示响应者中Clostridia/Monoglobus较多，非响应者中Hungatella较多，但整体预测效能缺失。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0d997db79f078889417976d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅基于基线血浆/粪便样本；未涉及干预后的动态变化；内毒素检测为首次在该人群中尝试，但结果不具预测性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"探讨了肠道屏障通透性（瓜氨酸、Zonulin、内毒素）与ICI反应的关系，结果为阴性。指出目前缺乏标准化的通透性测量方法和参考值。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2878a450f29ac8e861e46cc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文指出SCFA正常值未建立，肠道通透性测量缺乏标准化程序，这解释了为何不同研究间结果难以比较。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e0f2f1e541ed6711ababca57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文提到Akkermansia在其他癌症（如黑色素瘤）中与ICI反应正相关，但在本NSCLC研究中几乎不可检测或与反应无关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::96f7890c6c0f6aa3553389ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究结果为阴性，不能推断肠道微生物对ICI完全无效，而是表明在当前测量条件下（基线、特定组合）无法作为独立预测因子。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f79113c11be8141e2e665af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"结果受限于多种ICI药物的混合使用，不同药物可能对微生物群有不同影响，结论不能简单外推至单一ICI药物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e01cf6d45815d2847bb2cff7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肠道通透性指标的测量方法（如Zonulin、内毒素）在不同实验室间可能存在变异，需谨慎解读其绝对数值。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8bc7f60bf06e9375da80c6a7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"55名接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的III期或IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者；基线粪便和血液样本采集；使用16S rDNA扩增子测序（V3-V4区）分析微生物组成；使用气相色谱-质谱联用技术（GC-MS）定量粪便短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）；使用HPLC、化学发光法和ELISA分别测定血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、zonulin和内毒素；统计分析采用Pearson/Spearman相关性及整合变量分析。\",\n              \"finding\": \"未发现任何分析标记（包括细菌组成、短链脂肪酸丰度、血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、 zonulin和内毒素水平）与临床演变（ICI反应或irAE发生）存在相关性。尽管LEfSe分析显示 responder中 Clostridia和 Monoglobus较高， non-responder中 Hungatella较高，且 irAE患者中 Betaproteobacteria和 Enterococcus较高，但这些差异未能建立与反应或毒性的统计相关性。整体而言，微生物群落具有高度的个体特异性，但功能性和通透性表现出同质性。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为阴性结果的对照案例，展示在特定队列和方法下，肠道微生物组、短链脂肪酸及肠屏障指标与NSCLC免疫治疗反应无显著关联，平衡阳性发现。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究指出，尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群影响癌症免疫治疗反应，但在本研究的NSCLC队列中，未能识别出预测ICI反应或免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的生物标志物。作者强调，虽然微生物群落在组成上具有高度个体差异性，但其功能特性（如SCFA产生）和肠屏障通透性在患者间表现出同质性。此外，研究讨论了标准化方法的缺乏以及正常参考值的不确定性，这可能限制了生物标志物的发现能力。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"研究未提供具体的P值或效应量来量化“无相关性”的强度，仅陈述统计检验未检测到显著差异。\",\n            \"对于LEfSe发现的分类群差异为何未能转化为临床相关性，文中未深入探讨机制原因，仅指出需要更多研究。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b7607864c20694fa879e82d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Biomarkers of Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Non-Small-Cell Lung Cancer: Microbiota Composition, Short-Chain Fatty Acids, and Intestinal Permeability\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::190a2b1cc4763d7c54c3af3a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dbd886e8119b17e8ed8a2f8b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"55名接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的III期或IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者；基线粪便和血液样本采集；使用16S rDNA扩增子测序（V3-V4区）分析微生物组成；使用气相色谱-质谱联用技术（GC-MS）定量粪便短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）；使用HPLC、化学发光法和ELISA分别测定血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、zonulin和内毒素；统计分析采用Pearson/Spearman相关性及整合变量分析。\",\n              \"finding\": \"未发现任何分析标记（包括细菌组成、短链脂肪酸丰度、血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、 zonulin和内毒素水平）与临床演变（ICI反应或irAE发生）存在相关性。尽管LEfSe分析显示 responder中 Clostridia和 Monoglobus较高， non-responder中 Hungatella较高，且 irAE患者中 Betaproteobacteria和 Enterococcus较高，但这些差异未能建立与反应或毒性的统计相关性。整体而言，微生物群落具有高度的个体特异性，但功能性和通透性表现出同质性。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为阴性结果的对照案例，展示在特定队列和方法下，肠道微生物组、短链脂肪酸及肠屏障指标与NSCLC免疫治疗反应无显著关联，平衡阳性发现。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究指出，尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群影响癌症免疫治疗反应，但在本研究的NSCLC队列中，未能识别出预测ICI反应或免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的生物标志物。作者强调，虽然微生物群落在组成上具有高度个体差异性，但其功能特性（如SCFA产生）和肠屏障通透性在患者间表现出同质性。此外，研究讨论了标准化方法的缺乏以及正常参考值的不确定性，这可能限制了生物标志物的发现能力。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"研究未提供具体的P值或效应量来量化“无相关性”的强度，仅陈述统计检验未检测到显著差异。\",\n            \"对于LEfSe发现的分类群差异为何未能转化为临床相关性，文中未深入探讨机制原因，仅指出需要更多研究。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ef969d2f4e3a92c5b09a025\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"55名接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的III期或IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者；基线粪便和血液样本采集；使用16S rDNA扩增子测序（V3-V4区）分析微生物组成；使用气相色谱-质谱联用技术（GC-MS）定量粪便短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）；使用HPLC、化学发光法和ELISA分别测定血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、zonulin和内毒素；统计分析采用Pearson/Spearman相关性及整合变量分析。\",\n              \"finding\": \"未发现任何分析标记（包括细菌组成、短链脂肪酸丰度、血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、 zonulin和内毒素水平）与临床演变（ICI反应或irAE发生）存在相关性。尽管LEfSe分析显示 responder中 Clostridia和 Monoglobus较高， non-responder中 Hungatella较高，且 irAE患者中 Betaproteobacteria和 Enterococcus较高，但这些差异未能建立与反应或毒性的统计相关性。整体而言，微生物群落具有高度的个体特异性，但功能性和通透性表现出同质性。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为阴性结果的对照案例，展示在特定队列和方法下，肠道微生物组、短链脂肪酸及肠屏障指标与NSCLC免疫治疗反应无显著关联，平衡阳性发现。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究指出，尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群影响癌症免疫治疗反应，但在本研究的NSCLC队列中，未能识别出预测ICI反应或免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的生物标志物。作者强调，虽然微生物群落在组成上具有高度个体差异性，但其功能特性（如SCFA产生）和肠屏障通透性在患者间表现出同质性。此外，研究讨论了标准化方法的缺乏以及正常参考值的不确定性，这可能限制了生物标志物的发现能力。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"研究未提供具体的P值或效应量来量化“无相关性”的强度，仅陈述统计检验未检测到显著差异。\",\n            \"对于LEfSe发现的分类群差异为何未能转化为临床相关性，文中未深入探讨机制原因，仅指出需要更多研究。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ebdcd3094ca6a64d277cae9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb8cef2dc625a141ce84b692\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.3390/cancers16061144\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"8b3aa2316f5ec9089bf4d5f6cefbb1c1be74ad79\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n                \"title\": \"Biomarkers of Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Non-Small-Cell Lung Cancer: Microbiota Composition, Short-Chain Fatty Acids, and Intestinal Permeability\",\n                \"year\": \"2024\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"NSCLC 阴性结果研究，需确认其检测方法及队列特征，以作为平衡阳性发现的关键对照。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"55名接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的III期或IV期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者；基线粪便和血液样本采集；使用16S rDNA扩增子测序（V3-V4区）分析微生物组成；使用气相色谱-质谱联用技术（GC-MS）定量粪便短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）；使用HPLC、化学发光法和ELISA分别测定血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、zonulin和内毒素；统计分析采用Pearson/Spearman相关性及整合变量分析。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"未发现任何分析标记（包括细菌组成、短链脂肪酸丰度、血浆柠檬酸、抗柠檬酸抗体、 zonulin和内毒素水平）与临床演变（ICI反应或irAE发生）存在相关性。尽管LEfSe分析显示 responder中 Clostridia和 Monoglobus较高， non-responder中 Hungatella较高，且 irAE患者中 Betaproteobacteria和 Enterococcus较高，但这些差异未能建立与反应或毒性的统计相关性。整体而言，微生物群落具有高度的个体特异性，但功能性和通透性表现出同质性。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [], \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为阴性结果的对照案例，展示在特定队列和方法下，肠道微生物组、短链脂肪酸及肠屏障指标与NSCLC免疫治疗反应无显著关联，平衡阳性发现。\\\"}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究指出，尽管有证据表明肠道微生物群影响癌症免疫治疗反应，但在本研究的NSCLC队列中，未能识别出预测ICI反应或免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的生物标志物。作者强调，虽然微生物群落在组成上具有高度个体差异性，但其功能特性（如SCFA产生）和肠屏障通透性在患者间表现出同质性。此外，研究讨论了标准化方法的缺乏以及正常参考值的不确定性，这可能限制了生物标志物的发现能力。\\\", \\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"研究未提供具体的P值或效应量来量化“无相关性”的强度，仅陈述统计检验未检测到显著差异。\\\", \\\"对于LEfSe发现的分类群差异为何未能转化为临床相关性，文中未深入探讨机制原因，仅指出需要更多研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::efb0255c414ff070bab581f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0327\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2a114ae43a5c751a14df5a8e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f64b86f6332b5b10d7912848\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4b5f2a4e583d5e334c8406ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e375dcfa704548e4e1e2ce18\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作为一篇综述，本研究通过系统检索PubMed和Google Scholar数据库（关键词包括“gut microbiome and host immunity”等），筛选2011-2021年间发表的相关文献。内容综合分为三个主要部分：(1) 机制综述：从分子和细胞水平描述微生物-宿主免疫互作网络；(2) 临床转化综述：汇总关于FMT、益生菌、益生元及饮食干预的临床试验结果（引用Table 1列出具体试验）；(3) 批判性分析：讨论现有研究的局限性、安全性问题及未来方向。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::699ce05cd5b6d1ea0619d0b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的多维度机制框架（从黏膜屏障到全身免疫及TME重塑）；系统梳理了多种微生物干预策略（FMT、益生菌、益生元、饮食）的临床前及早期临床试验数据；指出了当前研究在标准化测序、供体选择及安全性方面的关键瓶颈。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，未进行新的实验验证；所引用的临床试验多为早期阶段（I/II期）或小样本，疗效证据尚不充分；不同研究间因队列差异、测序方法不同导致的结果不一致性未被完全解决；对于具体菌株或代谢物的因果机制，部分仍基于动物模型或观察性关联，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::598e775f94110c1118942162\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制层面\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物通过PRRs识别PAMPs激活先天免疫；通过GALT组织诱导Treg/Th17分化及SIgA产生；代谢物如SCFAs可进入循环调节全身免疫及TME中的巨噬细胞/DC功能；存在抗原交叉反应机制，针对细菌抗原的T细胞可能激活抗肿瘤反应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b9c08ebf69f13f06d0cf38c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"临床前显示FMT可将非响应者微生物转移给无菌小鼠从而恢复PD-1疗效；临床试验（如NCT03353402, NCT03341143）显示FMT联合PD-1抑制剂可使部分难治性黑色素瘤患者获得客观缓解，并改变肠道及肿瘤微环境的免疫细胞浸润。但存在严重不良事件风险（如耐药菌感染、死亡）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6a1935c1fa786f0d5c27a8ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"益生菌/菌群制剂\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定菌株（如Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus）联合ICI治疗在某些癌症（如肾癌、NSCLC）的临床试验中显示出改善ORR/PFS的趋势；某些菌株（如Blautia obeum）与不良预后或结肠炎风险增加相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::522c1a8223671dc609d86668\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"益生元/饮食\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗性淀粉（RS）等益生元促进有益菌生长及SCFA产生，增强化疗/放疗疗效并降低炎症因子；高纤维饮食与黑色素瘤患者更好的PD-1响应率相关；嘌呤核苷肌苷（Inosine）被鉴定为改善ICI疗效的关键代谢物。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::364b743ad363cbb93437d55d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::139e6b53b9edcfaa318dc0e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 肠道微生物组如何影响宿主免疫系统及抗肿瘤免疫？2. 肠道微生物组的组成和功能如何解释患者对ICIs治疗的异质性反应？3. 有哪些策略可以调节肠道微生物群以提高ICIs的疗效或减轻毒性？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f13f4ff62bafa7356cc1fc5d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肠道微生物组（Gut microbiome）与宿主免疫系统及癌症的相互作用，特别是其对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效的影响。涵盖机制探讨（先天/适应性免疫、肿瘤微环境）及干预策略（FMT、益生菌、益生元、饮食/生活方式）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::243c66c5adc1973443e09f34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结肠道微生物组在调节宿主免疫和癌症治疗反应中的最新知识。文章首先阐述了肠道微生物如何通过局部和全身途径影响宿主免疫系统（包括先天性和适应性免疫），并进一步讨论其在肿瘤微环境（TME）中对抗肿瘤免疫的作用。随后，文章评估了通过粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌、益生元以及饮食和生活方式改变来调节肠道微生物群以改善ICIs疗效的临床前证据和临床试验进展，并讨论了相关的安全性和未来挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::98b5ea781331e8ac5aa78af9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"所引用的临床试验多为早期探索性研究，样本量小，且结果存在异质性。不能直接推断所有微生物干预均有效，需结合其他研究确认特定菌株或策略的普适性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体干预策略及其临床现状。列举了FMT、益生菌（如V9, M9）、益生元（RS）及饮食（高纤维、发酵大豆）在多种实体瘤（黑色素瘤、肺癌、肠癌等）中的临床试验结果（引用Table 1）。指出高纤维饮食与PD-1响应率正相关，特定益生菌联合治疗可能改善ORR。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e09623aeb4d97eb72cc38807\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节（如具体的交叉反应肽段、Inosine的确切受体通路）主要基于动物模型（无菌小鼠、人源化小鼠）或体外研究。在人类患者中的直接因果证据仍在积累中，综述本身未提供新的机制验证数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物调节ICI疗效的潜在生物学机制。包括：1) 局部免疫：通过PRRs激活先天免疫，诱导Treg/Th17分化及SIgA产生；2) 全身免疫：代谢物（SCFAs, BAs, Inosine）进入循环调节免疫细胞；3) 肿瘤微环境：通过抗原交叉反应（Cross-reactivity）激活抗肿瘤T细胞，或通过细胞因子（TNFα, IL-12等）重塑TME。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfead1d510827947a5ceff6b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了肠道微生物组与宿主免疫系统的复杂互作网络，包括GALT组织、DCs、T细胞亚群（Treg, Th17）的功能及代谢物（SCFAs, AMPs）的作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9022ab3593d8b05c04816d74\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"指出当前领域面临的挑战：患者队列差异大、测序方法不统一（16S vs WGS）、参考数据库差异、FMT的安全性风险（耐药菌传播）、以及外源性因素（抗生素、饮食）的干扰。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4b778fc535f5dec927356858\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到了Blautia obeum与ICI结肠炎风险增加相关，Bacteroides具有双重效应；FDA关于FMT严重不良事件的警告。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1dc219a31203b26acd60013\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述涵盖多种癌症类型（黑色素瘤、肺癌、肠癌、肝癌等），在应用于特定固体瘤时需注意疾病特异性的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e591d4549916c26e538570d0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的临床疗效数据主要来自早期临床试验，效力证据等级有限，不可将其视为确证的临床指南。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::51e616dcfef51397e963d6e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分大量依赖动物模型推论，在人类身上的适用性需谨慎评估，特别是涉及具体菌株或代谢物的因果链条。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9b84e59ce8543ac4eeb0010e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同研究间的微生物组分析方法和定义可能存在差异，直接比较具体菌属丰度时需考虑技术偏差。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8cd1fc7eec45f6d5282bc5d2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0546\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b4fe98bf4129f2a01928c2de\",\n          \"snapshot::49f12e61cfb8da920f6cf528\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::113e9e24698e48b617801ee8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13d62ece3687ca3ff02b6c26\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ccd742ea527af43296074069\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1876e77f5afb8193a6a5257e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::999c7dbb4eb04f853f51ce68\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef45091c05d3c80087467567\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c4539dfe7511b5ee26afddc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f77d7a57b1c5af196e7ec273\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5bc8bb178fbe4aff2844625\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48e81723cf1694edffb2648d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f10ae71e3af0e5426782b275\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfc280fdf99afe8f46ce98b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ada46cc65142f66137be5912\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1440b6c81c7ea354a5c0604d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d56ff3d1c73603487584373\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2631f5b2da9f5640b19f7f49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a5656eba7a625dd6b12644d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f453542c412b162f0e6a8104\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5dfc4aabe5eadd2a5f8c90b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b12e17c00b7f89529c4a3847\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78071e0f85770a550546484c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0223323bb5c9771bfce68f11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::456d19e731aeafe092b5f494\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6edcdf66c26215bc9744d2b6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6daa66dcd75ef6a88df089e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::497b875e9b14be91a0c84f61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e34ebbbb34ba3c89d1c553df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::436fcf7aa325545c7b4b35ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1e65c84abaf39bc948ae4e34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b581c9a20631821c53f134ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bdf06d41fae85cb4002eea7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e56bf9725ffb96585d3b26d8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ffe022f4ac7a2eb8241e5388\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11e07541ccca87380640aaae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::163a7a8481c0223f6106b97e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"material_depth\": \"\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"reading_role\": \"\",\n                \"section_path\": [],\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::661ac39e317c4d00a2d636c4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4dd74fbdc2f421ab931a4cb0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::711d27360533c41d6d2ec36c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用范围综述方法论。使用PICO框架构建指导问题，在PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, Scopus, SciELO, LILACS五个数据库进行结构化搜索。纳入标准为涉及成年癌症患者、接受系统性肿瘤治疗、进行肠道微生物组分析并明确链接到治疗反应/毒性/预后的研究。排除儿科、仅放疗/手术、纯体外实验及2015年前文献。数据提取通过标准化表格进行，涵盖研究设计、人群特征、微生物分析方法、预测模型性能及主要结果。最终通过叙事综合法（narrative synthesis）对数据进行定性汇总，按癌症类型和治疗模式分类，重点区分“定量预测模型”与“微生物特征描述”，并识别知识空白和方法学局限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::011d8e1b72c422e144efa713\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了2015-2025年间肠道微生物组在肿瘤治疗反应中应用的全面地图，区分了预测模型开发与微生物特征描述两类证据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为范围综述，不进行质量评估或因果推断；未提供定量荟萃分析结果；所引用的原始研究多为小样本或回顾性，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素控制不足的风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47aa59edf8e80e7879afe702\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了微生物组预测模型在特定情境下（如尿路上皮癌、直肠癌）超越传统临床标记物的潜力，强调了菌株水平分辨率的重要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"不同研究的测序技术、生信流程和统计方法高度异质，导致直接比较困难；多数证据仍为关联性而非因果性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7ee2bfeae4e357feca73e50\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了临床转化的主要障碍：方法学标准化缺失、外部验证不足、机制不明及监管挑战。\",\n          \"limits\": \"未能提供具体的标准化协议建议或成本效益分析的详细数据；对真菌、病毒等非细菌微生物的作用探讨有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::83d1af535bb6a4c8baae2ee9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗，多中心队列及荟萃分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"菌株水平的微生物特征比临床因素更具预测力。Gunjur等(2024)发现针对联合ICI反应的菌株特征AUC为0.73，优于临床因素的0.56；但泛癌种通用特征在不同ICI方案间外推性较差（一致方案AUC 0.65 vs 不一致方案0.51）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa01327d182b7a35bd738a5f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"新辅助化疗，尿路上皮癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物组预测模型表现优于临床变量。Bukavina等(2024)开发的随机森林模型预测完全缓解（CR）的AUC为0.88，而临床因素仅为0.50；高拟杆菌属丰度与较差反应相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::65ce34ec16ea84186df5a999\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"同步放化疗，鼻咽癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"益生菌干预可降低毒性。Xia等(2021)的II期试验显示，益生菌鸡尾酒将3-4级口腔粘膜炎发生率从47.1%降至25%，并通过调节肠道菌群失调和增强免疫反应发挥作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdaca457d135841bbe395399\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"新辅助免疫放化疗，局部晚期直肠癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"物种水平模型具有高预测准确性。Yang等(2024)开发的SPEED模型在训练集AUC为98.8%，验证集为77.8%，用于预测病理完全缓解（pCR）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb0b5abe6bd93e8ca5e5c6b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"多种实体瘤，综述综合\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定菌属与疗效/毒性关联。双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等通常与ICI良好反应相关；梭杆菌、拟杆菌等在部分研究中与化疗耐药或毒性增加相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39bf57bd7ec01753d11856ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e3b08f72d596718e9bb782c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组衍生的生物标志物和预测模型在肿瘤治疗反应实践中具有何种临床潜力？具体动机在于应对癌症治疗的异质性响应、固有毒性及耐药性挑战，寻找能实现更精准患者选择和疗法优化的新型生物标志物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c91c85e8effd4baf32727a9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"成人癌症患者（涵盖结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、食管癌、尿路上皮癌等实体瘤），接受全身性肿瘤治疗（化疗、免疫检查点抑制剂ICIs、靶向治疗及联合方案）。研究范围聚焦于肠道微生物组作为生物标志物在预测治疗反应、毒性及疾病进程中的临床潜力，包括微生物特征识别和预测模型的开发/验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::738eff2017d024fc1b01f364\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇遵循JBI指南和PRISMA-ScR报告的范围综述（scoping review），旨在系统映射并批判性地描述当前关于肠道微生物组在肿瘤学中作为生物标志物的证据。作者检索了2015年至2025年间发表的20项相关研究，涵盖了观察性队列、临床试验和机制研究。综述重点分析了特定微生物类群如何影响免疫治疗和化疗的疗效，以及它们对治疗相关毒性的调节作用。研究发现，基于微生物组的预测模型在某些情况下优于传统临床标记物（如尿路上皮癌中AUC达0.88 vs 0.50），且特定干预（如益生菌）可减轻毒性。然而，综述也指出，由于方法学异质性、缺乏外部验证和机制理解不完整，这些模型的临床转化仍面临挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85d4c075f44e0f132e06caed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"预测模型的性能数据来自特定队列，外推性受限；FMT试验样本量小（n=15）；大多数关联证据来自观察性研究，不能直接证明因果关系。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体微生物特征和预测模型性能数据。包括：1) Gunjur等(2024)的多中心研究显示菌株水平特征对联合ICI反应的预测能力（AUC 0.73）优于临床因素；2) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Gopalakrishnan等(2018)综述指出的与良好ICI反应相关的菌属（双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等）；3) Davar等(2021)的临床试验显示FMT可使PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者获得客观缓解（20%）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::09a6b7bfdf51f2fbcab58d48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该综述主要归纳其他研究的机制发现，本身未提供新的机制实验数据；许多机制仍处于假说阶段，需结合原文献进一步验证；未详细阐述所有可能的代谢途径。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组调节ICI疗效的可能机制线索和间接证据。包括：1) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Chrysostomou等(2023)综述提到的免疫调节机制（如激活T细胞、NK细胞、I型干扰素通路）；2) McCulloch等(2022)观察到不利微生物特征与全身炎症（NLR升高）相关；3) Davar等(2021)发现FMT诱导CD8+ T细胞活化；4) 综述指出抗生素使用可能削弱ICI疗效，暗示生态依赖性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17e85bdc44e67b65e568505b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出当前证据的方法学异质性（样本采集、DNA提取、生信流程）、缺乏外部验证、小样本量导致的过拟合风险，以及因果关系的缺失。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d2018252fd4aee42531eb16\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述提到微生物组也影响化疗疗效（如梭杆菌促进耐药，拟杆菌改善某些化疗药效果）和毒性（如益生菌降低粘膜炎，特定菌属预测3-4级毒性）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93842ba0acb7c1623cffc35d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述提到微生物组特征在早期检测（结直肠腺瘤/癌，AUC 96%/87%）和疾病进展预测（如mCRC中乳酸杆菌与反应相关）中的潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::92203afa91a5d08ad9c31eae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述是范围综述，其结论基于对20项研究的叙事综合，而非定量荟萃分析。因此，其提供的“AUC”等性能指标应视为各独立研究的结果汇总，而非经过严格统计合并的估计值。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f144188f88dd66e6b5199a8c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述中引用的机制解释（如免疫激活、代谢产物作用）主要来自被综述的原始文献或评论文章，并非本综述作者的新发现。在引用时需明确来源。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bdb542a3b579fd596759670\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述强调“菌株水平”特征的重要性，但这主要基于Gunjur等(2024)的一项研究，其他多数研究停留在属或种水平。因此，菌株水平的优越性尚需更多证据支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2fa1a7af600d3f8db94c74b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述包含了一些非ICI治疗（如化疗、靶向治疗）的研究，在应用于回答ICI相关问题时，需注意区分不同治疗模式的微生物组相互作用差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f33418f66f54c2ba117b589d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述指出临床转化面临巨大挑战，因此在利用其提供的积极发现（如高AUC）时，必须同时强调其探索性质和缺乏外部验证的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::269a6177926dee975b0abb8c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31e54650732a464d8df54e97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::36b51e5503316dd632674da6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7f89d2bf4b616d931f1fb9c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法。作者综合了来自人类临床研究（队列研究、病例报告）和动物模型（无菌小鼠、抗生素处理小鼠、粪菌移植实验）的证据。分析路线包括：1) 梳理肠道黏膜免疫系统与全身免疫系统的连接机制；2) 归纳特定微生物分类群（Taxa）和代谢物的具体免疫调节功能；3) 评估微生物群组成/多样性与ICI疗效的临床相关性；4) 分析微生物群介导irAEs的病理生理机制；5) 审查FMT等干预措施的临床试验数据和安全性报告。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ecf6a34348bb3cf6a838167b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统整合了肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效的多维机制，包括特定菌株、代谢物、PRR信号通路及肠-肺轴交互作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给材料未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及偏倚风险评估方法；主要依赖已发表文献的叙述性综合，缺乏定量Meta分析。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f14b826214aac4ff650215f1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于FMT用于ICI相关irAEs的最新临床证据汇总，区分了其与传统IBD治疗的异同。\",\n          \"limits\": \"引用的FMT临床数据主要来自小型病例报告和观察性研究，缺乏大规模随机对照试验（RCT）支持；长期安全性和有效性数据不足。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5898fbd085784ac1d34d9d05\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了当前领域在标准化（样本采集、测序、生物信息分析）方面的挑战，强调了多组学和AI结合的必要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于不同微生物组合的具体协同效应及最佳干预时机等具体问题，仅提出方向性建议，未给出确切的临床操作指南。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::112d9578ce10a63f148df4a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"针对PD-1/PD-L1治疗的多种实体瘤（非小细胞肺癌、肾细胞癌、黑色素瘤）\",\n          \"finding\": \"应答者中Akkeermansia muciniphila的丰度显著高于无应答者；动物模型显示转移应答者粪菌可恢复ICI疗效，补充Akk可部分逆转抗生素导致的耐药。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c15cda0bf0ad48989d90f6c0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"涉及Bacteroides属的研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"证据不如Akkermansia robust；某些菌株（如B. fragilis）可能通过促进Th1反应增强抗CTLA-4疗效，但其他报告将高丰度Bacteroides与较低响应率或较短PFS关联，结果受肿瘤类型、宿主特征和菌株特异性影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a04d064eba5b73c0c8e327da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物群多样性指标\",\n          \"finding\": \"较高的Alpha多样性通常与更好的ICI响应和生存期相关，但并非所有研究都发现显著差异，表明单一生态参数不足以预测疗效，需结合功能基因和代谢组学。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6925d702ce7aa3def981ef82\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"代谢物调节机制\",\n          \"finding\": \"SCFAs（如丁酸）通过抑制HDAC和激活GPCRs调节T细胞代谢和分化；肌苷通过腺苷A2A受体促进Th1/Tc1极化；色氨酸代谢物通过AhR通路调节T细胞分化，而IDO介导的犬尿氨酸则抑制T细胞增殖。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11ba96025eeeabf75cbd48c4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT治疗难治性ICI相关结肠炎\",\n          \"finding\": \"短期疗效显著，多数病例报告显示临床症状迅速缓解，机制涉及局部炎症环境向抗炎状态转变（CD8+ T细胞减少，Treg增加）；但长期维持效果不确定，复发率可能介于溃疡性结肠炎（高复发）和复发性艰难梭菌感染（低复发）之间。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ab1ee6746be7b6db9b26c28\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b1b2b4a788459b5a51e65156\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs改变了实体瘤的治疗格局，但患者响应率不均且存在耐药性。肿瘤内在机制无法完全解释个体差异。本研究旨在厘清肠道微生物群如何作为“类器官”系统调节宿主免疫从而影响ICI疗效和毒性，并为开发基于微生物群的联合疗法提供理论依据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b64e8231f73616bfd2a80810\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"肠道微生物群（Gut Microbiome）与实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如PD-1/PD-L1、CTLA-4阻断剂）疗效及免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的关系。涵盖机制研究（细菌菌株、代谢物、PRR信号）、临床关联数据及转化策略（FMT）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b68c8ed6f12e1aedb57b11ad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结肠道微生物群影响ICIs疗效和毒性的现有机制证据，并探讨靶向微生物群的潜在治疗策略。文章首先阐述了肠道作为免疫界面的解剖学和生理学基础，随后详细讨论了特定有益菌属（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Bacteroides）及其代谢产物（短链脂肪酸SCFAs、肌苷、色氨酸代谢物）如何通过调节先天性和适应性免疫反应来增强抗肿瘤免疫。此外，文章分析了微生物群通过肠-肺轴等途径参与irAEs（特别是结肠炎和肺炎）的机制，并重点评估了粪便微生物移植（FMT）在治疗难治性ICI相关结肠炎中的临床应用现状、疗效、安全性及局限性。最后，文章指出了当前研究在标准化和可重复性方面的不足，并提出了未来结合多组学和人工智能进行精准医疗的方向。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8eb717837768e243082daa6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"临床关联多为观察性研究，因果链条在人类中尚未完全确立；不同癌症类型的结果可能存在异质性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效的临床关联证据和机制假说。具体包括：指出Akkermansia丰度与响应正相关，Bacteroides关联复杂，Alpha多样性具有预测潜力但非唯一指标。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a43c8c569fda1a67abdda11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节主要基于动物模型或体外研究，在人体内的确切效力和剂量依赖性尚需验证；部分代谢物（如肌苷）的作用具有情境依赖性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物群调节抗肿瘤免疫的具体分子和细胞机制。包括：1) 代谢物（SCFAs, Inosine, Tryptophan derivatives）对T细胞功能的重编程；2) PRR信号通路（TLR/NOD）对DC成熟和抗原呈递的增强；3) 肠-肺轴介导的远端器官免疫调节。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc672e268c1b1c1711f2806d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制多为推测性或基于间接证据，直接证明特定微生物导致特定irAEs的人类数据有限。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物群介导ICI毒性（irAEs）的机制解释，特别是结肠炎和肺炎。指出 dysbiosis 通过破坏屏障、改变代谢物和调节Th17/Treg平衡导致系统性炎症。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a81d31495d1e91c5f2dec021\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了FMT作为挽救疗法的短期有效性与长期不确定性，对比了UC和CDI的复发率以推断ICI相关结肠炎的预后。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c97341e86237730f0e4217ea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"指出当前研究在样本采集、测序和分析方法上的不标准化限制了可重复性，呼吁多中心长期队列和AI辅助的多组学研究。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0027ef883336f58d1bc2845a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要关注固体肿瘤，虽然提及了黑色素瘤和非小细胞肺癌，但不一定涵盖血液肿瘤或所有实体瘤亚型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31202fddebb7567b81ac4184\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"对于Bacteroides的作用，文中明确指出证据不一致，需谨慎解读，避免将其简单归类为“有益”或“有害”，应强调菌株特异性和情境依赖性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e1aed6019e6c69a7f1354c73\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT的数据主要来自病例报告和小型系列研究，证据等级较低，不能代表标准护理方案，仅作为探索性治疗手段讨论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc1be58fb8b1852c86b041b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分大量引用动物模型数据，在应用于人类临床解释时需注意种属差异和体内环境的复杂性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b461517bac77d0f0453474ea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0144\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::660a40da6b6fd9baeeaa7c45\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a8e041df58d3550e6b9670f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93cd882f4b9e181074968a9b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9be2b26a5b5e661354c8e867\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法。作者检索并筛选了关于肠道微生物群与ICI疗效关系的临床研究和临床前模型研究。通过分类整理不同干预措施（FMT、益生菌、饮食）的效果数据，对比反应者与不反应者的微生物组成差异，并从免疫微环境、系统性免疫、代谢产物及炎症通路等角度综合现有的机制解释文献，形成对领域现状的综合评述。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dbace3cc395d30e590ee9887\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统整合了肠道微生物群调节ICI疗效的临床证据（FMT、益生菌、饮食），并归纳了多层次的潜在生物学机制，为理解微生物-免疫互作提供了框架。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，依赖已发表研究的汇总，未进行新的原始数据分析；许多机制仍处于假设或初步验证阶段，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的最终确认；不同研究间微生物分析方法、人群异质性导致结果难以直接比较。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bc4daf35fe4d8c8c789ca825\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"临床观察与队列研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定微生物特征（如双歧杆菌、阿克曼菌、粪杆菌等）与ICI治疗的良好临床结局相关；抗生素诱导的菌群失调会损害ICI疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::798ebbfdd0dde971c93cb6a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自ICI反应者的粪便移植可改善黑色素瘤患者对PD-1抑制剂的响应，且安全性良好；健康供体的FMT联合PD-1抑制剂也显示出优于单药治疗的客观缓解率。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cfba85626e547e4916a78d0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"益生菌/菌群联合体\",\n          \"finding\": \"某些特定菌株（如CBM588中的丁酸梭菌）在随机对照试验中显示出提高客观缓解率和延长无进展生存期的潜力；但其他回顾性研究显示普通益生菌使用效果不一，甚至可能有害，表明菌株特异性至关重要。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f707e214620de54c46991b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"饮食干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"高纤维饮食与较长的无进展生存期相关，可能通过增加α多样性和有益菌丰度发挥作用；Omega-3摄入也与反应者相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10c3f5ac4aaead4dcaace7a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠道微生物可通过分子模拟引发T细胞交叉反应、激活PRRs促进树突状细胞成熟、产生短链脂肪酸等代谢物调节T细胞功能、以及通过易位影响肿瘤内微生物组等多种途径增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b58b7d1aae69de5bc159dab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b49504fca86b3118cf108630\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs改善了部分癌症患者的预后，但大多数患者仍无充分响应或产生耐药性，且现有生物标志物预测能力有限。肠道微生物群被认为是导致耐药的重要内在/外在因素，但其具体如何影响ICI疗效、哪些微生物特征有利、如何通过干预手段优化疗效以及其背后的生物学机制尚需系统总结。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ab5ca807f03f82ccece9553\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）在实体瘤治疗中的应用，重点聚焦于肠道微生物群对ICI疗效的影响、调节策略及其潜在机制。涵盖黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）、肾细胞癌等常见实体瘤类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ebada6823701e6a1c1f35757\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在系统梳理肠道微生物群与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效之间的关联。文章首先阐述了肠道微生物群作为影响ICI耐药性的关键因素，总结了反应者与非反应者之间微生物组成的差异，并定义了“有利”和“不利”的微生物特征。随后，文章详细评估了通过粪便微生物移植（FMT）、益生菌/菌群联合体以及饮食干预等手段调节肠道微生物群以增强ICI疗效的临床前和临床研究进展。此外，论文还探讨了这种调节作用对免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响，并归纳了包括分子模拟、模式识别受体激活、代谢物释放及肿瘤内微生物组调控在内的多种潜在作用机制。最后，文章指出了当前研究在供体选择、标准化、机制验证等方面的局限性，并提出了未来研究方向。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38a7687d425e30b58ce18d7c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"多数临床数据来自小规模试点研究或非随机对照试验；不同癌症类型的敏感性可能存在差异；益生菌效果高度依赖于具体菌株而非通用类别。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT、益生菌和饮食三种调节策略在实体瘤（主要是黑色素瘤和NSCLC）中的具体临床效果数据。例如，FMT来自反应者可提高客观缓解率；特定益生菌CBM588在RCT中显示优势；高纤维饮食与PFS延长相关。同时指出普通益生菌使用的争议性结果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c9b2027b3a0424f0cc72a3de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制基于小鼠模型或体外实验推断；人类体内确证证据有限；不同机制间可能存在重叠或协同，文中未明确量化各机制的贡献权重。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细列举了五种潜在机制：(1) 微生物蛋白模拟肿瘤抗原引发T细胞交叉反应；(2) 调节免疫检查点分子表达（如PD-L1/PD-L2）创造‘热’肿瘤微环境；(3) 激活PRRs（如TLR, NOD2, STING）促进DC成熟和T细胞活化；(4) 释放代谢物（SCFAs, 肌苷, TMAO等）调节全身和局部免疫；(5) 肠道微生物易位至肿瘤内部直接影响肿瘤内免疫微环境。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::433844f10ca6eac86c55b7cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中定义了‘有利’和‘不利’肠道微生物群的概念，并讨论了微生物多样性（Alpha diversity）的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::863ecbacd0d2327034a08a31\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了FMT和益生菌调节对免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的双重影响（既可能增强疗效也可能增加毒性风险）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e8ffa971de6b1f2d25d4aba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"强调需要更可靠的生物标志物来预测结果，需要标准化益生菌产品，以及真菌/病毒等其他微生物组成分的作用被低估。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::851cf2a4e35f0c392f38a720\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述涵盖的实体瘤类型有限，主要集中在黑色素瘤、NSCLC和肾细胞癌，对其他实体瘤（如结直肠癌、胰腺癌）的证据较少或仅为个案/早期研究，外推需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fc4f4250ca72e6fc61a9fbd4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的机制多为相关性或动物模型证据，不能直接等同于人类临床因果链条。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::98cdc11362da68ba08ff6f25\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"益生菌的研究结果存在显著异质性，取决于菌株特异性，不能将单一菌株的结果推广到所有益生菌产品。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::181f9e3fc4a7bb8677f3fb6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT供体的选择标准（反应者vs健康人）在不同研究中不一致，影响了结果的直接可比性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6555a560e2cc511b1d8753b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0161\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-132e8f9121acb3bc13bb\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::58905f5b7dead4e9c1149816\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::861d274a00593058a83f3e8e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ba33be4188920f512ede930\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::26c7b959b250209b6167c786\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a narrative review of existing literature, including preclinical mouse models (germ-free, antibiotic-treated, recolonization experiments) and human clinical studies (retrospective analyses, small prospective cohorts, FMT trials). They categorized findings by clinical outcome (response vs. non-response, colitis vs. no colitis), identified key microbial taxa and metabolites, and synthesized proposed biological mechanisms (antigen-dependent vs. independent). The review also discusses methodological challenges such as sequencing heterogeneity and confounding factors like geography and diet.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32466a7665abc89a632ca779\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Synthesizes fragmented preclinical and clinical evidence into a coherent framework distinguishing antigen-dependent and antigen-independent mechanisms of microbiome-ICI interaction.\",\n          \"limits\": \"The review acknowledges significant inconsistency in identified bacterial taxa across studies due to technical heterogeneity, population differences, and tumor type specificity; it does not resolve these discrepancies but highlights them as areas needing larger standardized studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d35932d00288b5b99db6d5f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific metabolites (SCFAs, tryptophan derivatives, inosine) and their associations with ICI outcomes, providing a basis for metabolic biomarker development.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Most metabolite data come from small cohort studies or single centers; causal relationships and reproducibility across diverse populations remain unconfirmed.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::89dc6c4299ab04118d42ef2e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Highlights the potential of FMT as a therapeutic strategy to overcome ICI resistance and treat colitis, based on early-phase clinical trials.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Current FMT evidence is limited to small case series and pilot studies; safety, optimal donor selection, and long-term efficacy are not yet established.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::085aa5d13333e18f891b3108\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical mouse models (SPF vs GF, antibiotic treatment)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Intact commensal microbiome is required for anti-tumor efficacy of anti-CTLA-4 antibodies; germ-free or antibiotic-depleted mice show compromised responses.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e22d936b9e5d3051a9e2aeb4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Human metastatic melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4\",\n          \"finding\": \"Higher abundance of Faecalibacterium prausnitzii and Gemmiger formicilis associated with positive response; Bacteroides associated with poor response.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa01a377236c40b93227d94e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Human advanced NSCLC or urothelial carcinomas treated with ICIs\",\n          \"finding\": \"Increased relative abundances of Akkermansia muciniphila and Enterococcus hirae associated with clinical response.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07a943c867a88980d90a169c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Human solid tumors treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"Higher fecal short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), particularly propionate, associated with longer progression-free survival in some cohorts, though conflicting results exist for butyrate and other SCFAs across different cohorts.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fa42d4d99ed38acb34c1d37b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients receiving broad-spectrum antibiotics prior to or during ICI therapy\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use is consistently associated with reduced ICI efficacy, shorter overall survival, and shorter progression-free survival.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dedbea0d3515dd54bf16aa5d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI-associated colitis pathogenesis\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific bacteria (e.g., Bacteroides fragilis, Burkholderia cepacia) may protect against colitis by promoting regulatory T cells; conversely, increases in Firmicutes have been linked to higher incidence of colitis.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c78e7cc967833bf2f392d7c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways\",\n          \"finding\": \"Two major mechanisms identified: (1) Antigen-independent: Microbes modulate innate/adaptive immunity (e.g., dendritic cell activation, CD8+ T cell infiltration); (2) Antigen-specific: Molecular mimicry where microbial epitopes cross-react with tumor neoantigens.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c29dfd46f6d921851086de8c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d79e2be028afafd60ebc2af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"How does the intestinal microbiome modulate the efficacy and toxicity of ICIs? What are the specific microbial signatures and mechanisms involved, and how can these insights be translated into clinical biomarkers or therapies?\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d968e3d265dd2454d8368edd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the role of the intestinal microbiome and microbial-derived metabolites in modulating responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in cancer patients, specifically addressing efficacy outcomes (tumor response, survival) and toxicities (immune-related adverse events like colitis). It covers preclinical mouse models and retrospective/prospective human clinical studies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c9ca196e0f93ee8c629cc194\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This paper reviews the emerging evidence linking the gut microbiome to the efficacy and toxicity of immune checkpoint blockade immunotherapy. It synthesizes findings from preclinical models and clinical studies to identify specific bacterial taxa and metabolites associated with ICI response or resistance. The authors discuss two main mechanistic categories: antigen-independent modulation of innate and adaptive immunity, and antigen-specific cross-reactivity between microbial and tumor antigens. Additionally, the review examines the negative impact of antibiotic use on ICI efficacy and the potential of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) to restore responsiveness or treat colitis. It highlights inconsistencies across studies regarding specific beneficial bacteria and calls for larger prospective interventional trials to establish microbiome-based biomarkers and therapeutic strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15f73eb5eadb303dd3b9f876\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are inconsistent across studies; many findings are from retrospective or small prospective cohorts. Causal direction is often inferred rather than proven. Specific taxa may vary by tumor type and geography.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a catalog of specific bacterial taxa (e.g., Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium) and metabolites (propionate, inosine) associated with improved ICI response in various solid tumors, along with taxa linked to poor response (Bacteroides, Ruminococcus obeum). Also details the negative impact of broad-spectrum antibiotics on ICI outcomes.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b52a2a2c18a4fca342b2c728\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanistic evidence is largely derived from preclinical models or small-scale human studies. The prevalence and clinical significance of antigen mimicry are still being elucidated. Inconsistencies in human data limit definitive mechanistic claims.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Outlines two distinct mechanistic pathways: (1) Antigen-independent modulation via innate/adaptive immune cell engagement (e.g., DC activation, CD8+ T cell infiltration); (2) Antigen-specific cross-reactivity between microbial and tumor neoantigens. Discusses how specific bacteria might promote regulatory T cells to prevent colitis.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::825500cc93825fbbc3024cf3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Introduction to ICIs, their mechanism (blocking inhibitory pathways), and the problem of heterogeneous response and immune-related adverse events (colitis).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9ae21607fe4cc933f2b679c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Acknowledgment of sequencing center heterogeneity, geographical/population differences, and the need for large-scale prospective studies similar to GWAS.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0603b6d101f75d1ebc9a2a83\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Table 2 listing ongoing trials investigating microbiome modification (e.g., potato starch supplement), FMT for colitis, and biomarker identification.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c3e02d1c5d2220b47046098f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers both preclinical (mouse) and clinical (human) data; distinctions must be maintained when attributing findings to human applicability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d8ed7fc7fc933274280a7ac1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Identified bacterial taxa and metabolites show inconsistency across studies; do not present them as universal predictors without noting context-dependence (tumor type, geography, methodology).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a66e1342c7b2e0deef60e823\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic explanations (especially antigen mimicry) are presented as emerging hypotheses supported by limited evidence; avoid overstating their generalizability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2e125b37f8b82c5131d48d04\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT efficacy is based on very small pilot studies; conclusions about its therapeutic potential are preliminary and controversial.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cbd95c7db063421bbc9468d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::16691695321f5acfe09a283c\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32afad53dcf43f0b6c9b72e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0bfb82785a3c48347dccebf7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::df7c1c8cdb1b19415f16bd7c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性综述方法，梳理已发表的临床试验数据（包括已完成和正在进行的研究）。作者按干预类型（益生菌、菌群组合、FMT）分类整理证据，对比各试验的设计、患者人群、疗效指标（ORR, mPFS）及不良事件。同时，结合讨论部分，分析导致临床结果不一致的原因（如物种特异性、定植能力、抗生素预处理的影响），并评估当前监管框架和研究方法论（如小鼠模型的局限性）对转化研究的制约。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad144ff01b7112fa74c4f766\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于微生物疗法作为ICI辅助治疗的全景式临床证据汇总，特别是区分了益生菌、菌群组合和FMT在不同实体瘤中的表现差异。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对机制的解释主要基于作者对现有文献的综合推断，具体分子通路尚不明确；所引用的临床试验多为小样本或早期阶段，统计效力有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::18fce5dbd3407432b774c9dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了当前领域面临的非科学障碍，如监管标准不适用于复杂微生物产品、患者招募困难及抗生素预处理策略的潜在风险。\",\n          \"limits\": \"这些观点属于领域内的共识性讨论，并非该综述独有的实证发现；对于如何解决这些系统性问题，仅提出了方向性建议（如AI建模、标准化供体筛选），未提供具体解决方案。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e026da3395f4a6e48096eefc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用单一或少数菌株益生菌（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在某些特定癌种（如转移性肾细胞癌）中显示出较高的ORR提升（58%-74% vs 对照20%），但在其他癌种（如微卫星稳定型结直肠癌）中效果不佳或无效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ffe37d5b7bd2ed2749dc96b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用多菌株微生物菌群组合（如MET4, SER-401, VE800）\",\n          \"finding\": \"结果高度异质。MET4在部分队列中显示潜在获益，但受限于招募失败；SER-401因早期终止且初步数据显示疗效不优于安慰剂而终止；VE800整体ORR极低（1.9%），仅在黑色素瘤亚组中观察到一定益处。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e58ae790bec32ee11a9df4c4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在多种难治性实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、MSI-H癌症等）中显示出一致的积极信号，ORR普遍较高（20%-77%），且安全性总体可控，提示其可能具有广谱抗肿瘤活性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1cdfbbb48f5f9c98936fc044\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制研究与模型转化\",\n          \"finding\": \"目前缺乏明确的单一因果细菌物种；机制涉及T细胞浸润、代谢物（如短链脂肪酸）产生及免疫基因集变化。小鼠模型与人类微生物组差异巨大，限制了直接外推。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e9de08819bb3b4ed6078f1fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2827d99d3dcf98657562d9b2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICI疗法改变了部分实体瘤的治疗格局，但其对“冷”肿瘤或无响应患者的效果有限。本研究旨在解决如何安全有效地将微生物疗法作为ICI的辅助手段，以扩大受益人群并克服耐药性问题。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::897420d152a1f4691a65b58e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"固体肿瘤患者中，肠道微生物群作为免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）辅助治疗的临床前与临床研究现状。涵盖益生菌、微生物菌群组合及粪便微生物移植（FMT）三种主要干预手段。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10082b6cc311135dbfe6dcf1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在评估通过调节肠道微生物群来增强固体肿瘤免疫治疗疗效的潜力。文章系统回顾了基于单菌株/有限混合物的益生菌（如CBM588、EDP1503）、多菌株微生物菌群组合（如MET4、SER-401、VE800）以及全环境粪便微生物移植（FMT）在联合ICI治疗中的临床试验结果。研究重点分析了不同干预策略在客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（mPFS）及安全性方面的表现，并探讨了从动物模型到人体转化的挑战、监管障碍、患者招募困难以及现有机制理解的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3a7be2d0ab0883257f020f7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些数据来自小样本早期临床试验，存在选择偏倚和统计效力不足的问题。不能据此断定某种特定菌株在所有情况下均有效或无效。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了三类微生物干预策略在多种实体瘤中与ICI联用的临床疗效对比数据。具体而言，指出FMT在多种难治性肿瘤中表现出较一致的ORR提升（20-77%），而益生菌和菌群组合的效果则呈现高度的癌种特异性和菌株依赖性（如CBM588在mRCC有效但在MSS CRC无效，VE800整体无效）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e7a08fe8d3267d2e0ff0d6a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述多为相关性观察或基于动物模型的推测，文中明确承认“大部分未知”。不能将这些关联视为已证实的因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"讨论了微生物调节ICI疗效的可能机制线索，包括T细胞浸润增加、抗原呈递细胞（APCs）积累、IL-8产生髓系细胞减少以及短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）等代谢物的作用。同时指出目前缺乏单一因果物种的证据，倾向于网络效应和功能冗余。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6150bc781f7918a9915bfded\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了ICI的作用原理（PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4抑制，T细胞增殖）及其在“冷”肿瘤中的局限性。定义了“热”与“冷”肿瘤的概念，并引入肠道微生物群作为潜在的共治疗手段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf5d9ab2e65ee7a5c7b0216a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"批评了传统还原论方法（寻找单一因果基因/蛋白）在微生物研究中的失效，提出需要机器学习/AI模型来处理微生物组的复杂性，并指出小鼠模型与人类微生物组的差异是转化研究的瓶颈。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c024714554d6bd9bfa71d6cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"详细描述了微生物疗法在临床试验中面临的监管难题（难以标准化复现的产品）、患者招募困难以及抗生素预处理带来的潜在危害（如SER-401试验中的负面结果）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb21724cdddb728c61b9904e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要关注细菌疗法，虽提及真菌、古菌和病毒，但未深入展开，阅读时需限定在细菌层面。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b5bf19d3d412ec4c9e5076d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所有临床数据均为早期阶段（Phase I/II）或小样本研究，结果存在较大不确定性，不可将其视为确证性证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3da6b2c628061aac471cc4ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者强调FMT效果较好，但这可能源于FMT引入了更多样的菌群而非特定成分，需谨慎归因。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aff3ce7e2f53b8c83f7866ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的“抗生素预处理”在SER-401试验中被证明可能有害，这一反面案例对于设计微生物干预方案具有重要警示意义。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c1253fcac84e6039a9d7c2a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39e9ed6abcfb0ce941cea36a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a7abaa8d4970802424195dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::582929f6f34e9511832eb25d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用系统综述和荟萃分析方法。首先进行系统性文献检索，筛选评估基线肠道微生物群、FMT、益生菌/益生元干预或抗生素暴露的研究。随后使用随机效应模型汇总估计总生存期（OS）和无进展生存期（PFS）的风险比（HR），以及缓解率和irAEs的比值比（OR）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d81056a067318e687a986ca0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于肠道微生物群关键特征（特定菌属、多样性、抗生素影响、FMT效果）与ICIs疗效及安全性之间关联的定量综合证据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代异质性分析结果、发表偏倚评估细节、具体癌症类型的亚组分析结果、irAEs的具体统计数值（仅提及关联性）、以及纳入研究的原始数据质量评估标准。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::865c3fce85bd3a3a7bb8c697\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"特定细菌属富集（Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium longum, Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）\",\n          \"finding\": \"与改善的总生存期（HR 0.62, 95% CI 0.51-0.76）和无进展生存期（HR 0.69, 95% CI 0.55-0.83）显著相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55e5fca6e95dbafa7b97ba97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在ICI治疗前或期间暴露于抗生素\",\n          \"finding\": \"与较差的总生存期相关（HR 1.84, 95% CI 1.45-2.34）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::afa5de82594d6caa0498c1c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"接受来自反应者的FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"表现出更高的客观缓解率（OR 2.91, 95% CI 1.48-5.73）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8304fac36c52270463706836\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"比较响应者与无响应者\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者的微生物多样性指数 consistently higher（持续更高）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39e500e67c1cea96462d0aaf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf1d46b1c9816d089c247528\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管临床前和临床研究提示特定细菌类群可能影响ICIs的疗效和irAEs，但这些关联的幅度和一致性尚不明确。本研究旨在量化肠道微生物群组成及其调控对ICIs治疗疗效和毒性谱的具体影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2f51eb111c2ace15d2475862\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"癌症患者（特别是接受免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者）的肠道微生物群组成、干预措施及其与疗效和不良事件的关系。涵盖的研究类型包括观察性研究（基线菌群、抗生素暴露）、干预性研究（FMT、益生菌/益生元）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8bd32a4a71acaf80a8edd654\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文是一篇系统综述和荟萃分析，旨在评估肠道微生物群对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。作者通过系统检索PubMed、Embase、Web of Science和Cochrane Library数据库（截至2025年3月），纳入了38项涉及5,642名患者的研究。研究重点分析了特定细菌属（如Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium longum、Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）的富集、抗生素使用、供体反应者粪便微生物移植（FMT）以及微生物多样性指数与总生存期（OS）、无进展生存期（PFS）、客观缓解率（ORR）及irAEs之间的关联。结果显示，有益菌富集与改善生存预后显著相关，而抗生素暴露则与较差的生存结果相关，FMT从反应者来源可显著提高缓解率。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d515e81ecce4092cc77829d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅展示关联，不直接提供分子机制；未区分不同肿瘤类型间的差异；未提供irAEs的具体效应量数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了特定细菌属（Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium）富集与ICIs疗效提升（OS, PFS）的正向关联证据；提供了抗生素暴露与疗效下降的负向关联证据；提供了FMT提高ORR的证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6b402a143e9e52a21f1a8a4b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"本综述本身未深入阐述具体的分子或细胞机制（如抗原呈递、T细胞浸润等），因此不能直接用于回答机制问题，只能作为机制研究的动机或验证目标。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"虽然主要关注临床结局关联，但通过指出特定菌属和多样性的作用，间接指向了可能的机制路径（如免疫激活）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e78858b2e1123d4265b08dbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"确认肠道微生物群是ICIs疗效的关键决定因素，且存在可量化的关联。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f23e8af78b1f515d19225376\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"抗生素使用的负面效应（HR 1.84）与有益菌的正面效应形成对比。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::22ade239973f63ac1cc2ad87\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为荟萃分析结果，反映的是群体水平的统计关联，不能直接推断个体因果机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f416788f290cefd8da15ac8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"摘要未提供各纳入研究间异质性（I^2等）的具体数值，解读效应量时需考虑研究间差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db09b0238c5e110876ebe550\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"未明确说明是否针对特定实体瘤进行了分层分析，若综述关注特定癌种，需核实此处的结论是否适用于所有实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::751f28ea1ac600e31a54ae09\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"irAEs的结果在摘要中仅定性提及“impact”，缺乏具体OR值和置信区间，无法用于精确量化毒性风险。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::101242efec5527ae977e69ab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::66afcfe719fb8b5ee6396eb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0eb61fe9830b1063300638cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e36852e039a578ad56dc1947\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfaa65a3320dc440ddff00ad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a narrative synthesis of existing literature. They categorized findings into potential benefits (positive clinical responses in melanoma, CRC, etc.) and failures (e.g., SER-401 trial). Mechanisms were analyzed through host physiology alterations (microbiota diversity/composition, metabolites like SCFAs and bile acids, TME immune cell infiltration, signaling pathways). Optimization strategies were derived from donor screening criteria, functional vs. composition-based selection, and monitoring methods. Future perspectives were outlined based on identified gaps in current knowledge.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::95ea94d27b2d7b2268bfea91\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a structured overview of the heterogeneous clinical outcomes of FMT-ICI combination therapy across different cancer types.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data or perform a systematic quantitative meta-analysis; conclusions are based on synthesized observations from cited studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::450a76879e9b6be3204aedb4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Elucidates complex, multi-level mechanisms linking gut microbiota to ICI response, highlighting both beneficial and detrimental pathways.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts; causal relationships in humans require further validation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9b598e37442cf0b01ffd531d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies critical variables (donor selection, recipient status, protocol details) that contribute to outcome variability.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Standardized protocols for donor selection and FMT administration are not yet established, limiting direct clinical translation recommendations.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11c4feb5b5ae93fe26823491\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"In responders to anti-PD-1 therapy (e.g., melanoma, MSS-mCRC)\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT increases gut microbial diversity and enriches beneficial taxa (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium), leading to enhanced CD8+ T cell infiltration, reduced immunosuppressive cells (Tregs, MDSCs), and improved clinical outcomes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::77f7f442b2ee33b41d52bb77\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"In non-responders or specific trials (e.g., NCT03817125 with SER-401)\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT or defined bacterial formulations may fail to improve or even worsen outcomes, potentially due to the expansion of immunosuppressive cells, activation of resistance pathways, or introduction of harmful metabolites/bacteria.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c7718994e5ccb908e7d025e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic level\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT modulates ICI efficacy via multiple pathways: altering microbiota composition/diversity, producing metabolites (SCFAs can be both beneficial and immunosuppressive; bile acids like DCA can promote tumor growth), reshaping the TME (increasing effector T cells, decreasing suppressive myeloid cells), and modulating signaling pathways (TLR, Wnt/β-catenin).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cd8d7b2aff300bc3e39abfe6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2f7f34d1e2f3b372fe06493a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To address the inconsistency in clinical outcomes when combining FMT with ICIs, elucidate the underlying mechanisms of this interaction, identify key factors influencing efficacy, and provide a framework for optimizing FMT strategies to enhance immunotherapy response.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::307ba8b829e2c5c2fed7647d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the integration of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) for cancer treatment. It covers clinical evidence from various solid tumors (melanoma, colorectal cancer, etc.), preclinical mechanistic studies, and optimization strategies for FMT protocols.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bdd4c29ead36b61ef77d66e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This is a comprehensive narrative review that critically examines the controversial effects of combining FMT with ICIs. It synthesizes evidence from clinical trials and preclinical studies to explain why FMT sometimes enhances ICI efficacy while other times shows no benefit or adverse effects. The paper outlines mechanisms involving gut microbiota modulation, metabolite profiles, and tumor microenvironment changes, and discusses factors influencing outcomes such as donor selection, recipient characteristics, and administration protocols. It concludes by proposing future research directions including large-scale trials, multi-omics integration, and alternative microbiome-based therapies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5013ece2973d969d51eb7c45\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Evidence is drawn from various trial phases and tumor types; generalizations across all solid tumors should be cautious due to varying baseline microbiomes and tumor immunogenicity.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence showing that FMT can enhance ICI efficacy in specific solid tumors (melanoma, MSS-mCRC) by correlating with increased microbial diversity and beneficial taxa enrichment. Also reports cases where FMT failed or showed adverse effects.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07684cdaa7711484a96a6e52\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Some mechanisms are primarily supported by preclinical mouse models; human validation is ongoing. The dual role of certain metabolites (e.g., SCFAs) means effects are context-dependent.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details specific mechanisms: 1) Modulation of gut microbiota diversity/composition affecting T cell function. 2) Metabolite-mediated effects (SCFAs enhancing CD8+ T cells but also promoting Tregs; bile acids promoting tumor growth). 3) TME remodeling (increased CD8+ T cells, decreased Tregs/MDSCs). 4) Signaling pathway modulation (TLR, Wnt/β-catenin).\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2226fca183a362e244126599\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Comparison of FMT with other microbiome interventions (prebiotics, postbiotics, defined consortia) and discussion of alternatives like SER-401 and MET4.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21da90be60b5d73d7b8ff795\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion on regulatory frameworks, donor screening standards, and long-term safety assessments.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dd15735166da05292e878072\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers multiple cancer types, not exclusively solid tumors; ensure relevance to the user's focus on solid tumors is maintained.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9bcc0d92e9bead3c890478c5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic claims often rely on preclinical data; distinguish between observed associations in humans and proposed mechanisms from animal models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31c84a6ae14740360e96957e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The term 'controversial' reflects mixed results; avoid interpreting negative results as definitive proof of inefficacy without considering confounding factors (donor, protocol, patient status).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b24a190d28e263126fc08053\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0573\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fd\",\n          \"snapshot::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c\",\n          \"snapshot::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bb6ad04fca560d182cec1f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::23b203078daf59896544114b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f68ab6ce48799e6ca1058cd3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的IIa期篮子试验设计。纳入标准包括ICI治疗后疾病进展、ECOG评分0-1及可测量病灶。供体需为ICI长期响应者（>12个月响应）。干预措施包括基线后第1周和第5周通过结肠镜进行两次FMT，随后在第14、30、78周可通过灌肠进行最多三次补充FMT。ICI治疗保持不变或重新引入。主要终点评估安全性和ORR（基于iRECIST）。次要终点包括可行性、临床获益率、无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、微生物定植（16S rRNA测序）、免疫反应（质谱流式细胞术分析PBMCs）及生物标志物（血清细胞因子）。统计分析采用描述性统计、Kaplan-Meier生存分析及Cox比例风险模型探索免疫特征与预后的关联，未进行多重检验校正。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e4bb77f5eebd2aa771b705\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，使用ICI响应者供体的FMT是安全和可行的。提供了关于FMT后微生物定植动力学（短暂性）和系统性免疫景观（髓系抑制与T细胞活化）的详细生物标志物数据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量小（n=12），试验因入组缓慢提前终止。单臂设计无法确立因果关系，缺乏对照组。未能实现预期的临床疗效（无ORR），限制了对其机制解释的确定性。结果可能受到快速进展性疾病背景的影响，未能在足够长的时间内观察FMT的潜在延迟效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59a3a7b73308240f96ffb39c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"12名ICI耐药晚期实体瘤患者，接受来自ICI响应者的FMT联合ICI治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT安全性良好，无严重FMT相关不良事件导致停药，但50%患者出现免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），多数为轻度。客观缓解率（ORR）为0%，中位PFS为1.5个月，中位OS为10.1个月。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da136020eae35e8a2dfc6af1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"首次FMT后一周，大多数受体的微生物组向供体方向偏移（定植成功），但这种相似性在后续时间点大多下降，表明定植多为暂时性。仅1名获得临床获益的患者实现了持久的供体-受体微生物相似性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0836a8c74dab91d3a0b4f4ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"免疫微环境分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"基线时高度分化的T细胞环境（CD8+效应记忆T细胞和TEMRA）与改善的PFS和OS相关；而髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型预后较差。CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平随时间增加，高水平的CD14+单核细胞与较短的PFS和OS相关。这些免疫特征与预后的关联在使用ICI治疗起始日期重新计算时依然成立，提示其反映的是宿主对免疫治疗的固有反应能力，而非FMT的直接因果效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa9a46960936e1395aed9137\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bbf51165ebd9be173e979c8e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"早期研究表明FMT可能逆转ICI耐药，但其适用性在其他肿瘤类型中尚不明确，且关于患者选择、供体选择及给药方案的问题仍未解决。本研究试图回答：在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，重复FMT是否安全可行，以及是否能通过微生物定植和免疫重塑来恢复ICI的疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb7c28aa6d5a8423ece0135\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤（黑色素瘤、头颈部鳞癌、肾细胞癌、微卫星不稳定性高胰腺癌）中免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药或进展的患者，评估来自ICI长期响应者的粪菌移植（FMT）联合ICI治疗的安全性和有效性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0ae5567370b869d8e867f54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究是一项单臂IIa期篮子试验（MITRIC），旨在验证通过FMT调节肠道微生物群能否克服已建立的ICI耐药性。研究纳入了12名在转移性阶段对ICI治疗进展的患者，使用ICI长期响应者作为供体，给予患者最多五次FMT（前两次通过结肠镜，后续通过灌肠），并继续原有ICI治疗。主要终点为FMT相关不良事件和客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示FMT安全性良好，但未能观察到客观肿瘤反应（ORR为0%），仅5名患者达到疾病稳定。尽管缺乏总体疗效证据，研究发现FMT诱导了短暂的微生物定植，且外周血中的免疫细胞特征（如分化T细胞与髓系细胞的平衡）与生存期显著相关，但这些免疫特征似乎更多反映疾病本身状态而非FMT的特异性干预效果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb862a9266fa81e78d243db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于ICI耐药/进展人群，不能外推至一线治疗场景。样本量极小，结果可能存在偶然性，但趋势明确。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT在广泛ICI耐药实体瘤队列中的真实世界疗效数据：ORR为0%，中位PFS仅为1.5个月。这表明在非选择性、快速进展的耐药人群中，FMT联合ICI并非有效的挽救疗法。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b6331b5c08533653c791a8b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"免疫关联分析为探索性，未校正多重检验，且缺乏对照组，无法证明FMT改变了这些免疫特征从而改善了预后。仅描述了相关性，未证明因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT干预后系统性免疫景观的变化及其与预后的关联：(1) FMT诱导的微生物定植多为暂时性，仅持久定植者与临床获益相关；(2) 基线高分化T细胞表型预示更好预后，而高髓系细胞（CD14+）和高IL-8水平预示不良预后；(3) 这些免疫特征似乎反映了宿主固有的免疫反应能力，而非FMT直接重塑的结果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38d60665b7ae5ef0786b2453\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究讨论了使用ICI响应者作为供体的局限性（微生物组成差异大），以及不同研究间供体数量（单供体vs多供体）对结果的潜在影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fd300138b8a38b7318335545\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"比较了结肠镜给药（前两次）和灌肠给药（后续）的可行性及耐受性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1c0f5c1558648ba8264b5ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的阴性结果主要归因于患者群体的快速进展特性和小样本量，不应将其解读为FMT在所有情况下均无效，而应视为特定情境下的失败尝试。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::602293d8d060926ae50da0a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"免疫生物标志物的发现是探索性的，且可能与ICI治疗本身的效应混淆，需谨慎解读其作为FMT特异性机制的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d04d310196a133922df7cbd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物定植的暂时性并不必然意味着临床无效，因为唯一获益患者的持久定植提示了两者间的潜在联系，但这仅是个案观察。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::224d056381af07f5414ea73a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::49d98c7f1b143d31120d9835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74660f9101b72ae9aef33244\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::474c7e797e5493a25ea68330\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6a147f41d39b13a9ab869ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6597e99daf38ab354bfeeb09\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe5e2b03a837721c9a331e97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b8ed4ce6c977fbd7aecee5c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::648ccd951a6ed0f6c928cb17\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::748f5657e9b651a2113dca8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::acc00d9cd4f644b83ac0cda1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\\\", \\\"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\\\", \\\"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Baruch et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R19\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Davar et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R18\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Kim et al. (2024)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R20\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\\\n\\\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\\\n\\\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\\\n\\\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\\\", \\\"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\\\", \\\"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d15b90b1b4387e8af2a1be3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16d054e681e54f8a54f2fd2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4a19a0d9b7f5acaad003b10\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6b3c39236af481f48796c5a5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a narrative review, the authors synthesized existing literature on ICI-induced irAEs. The structure follows a logical progression: first, elucidating core immunopathological mechanisms (T-cell, B-cell, cytokine, monocyte axes); second, analyzing multidimensional risk factors (host, environment, treatment, tumor, genetics); third, detailing clinical features, grading, and management strategies for irAEs across major organ systems; and fourth, proposing future research directions focusing on shared mechanisms, predictive models, and optimized intervention strategies. The approach relies on summarizing clinical studies, experimental data, and meta-analyses cited in the references.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b674d56e73dd08f9bbfecb45\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive, up-to-date synthesis of the multifaceted mechanisms (cellular and molecular) underlying irAEs, integrating T-cell, B-cell, cytokine, and monocyte pathways.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a review, it does not present new primary experimental data or validate predictive biomarkers clinically; it summarizes existing evidence which may be heterogeneous.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e03a2182581575edeadacd6c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Offers a detailed, organ-system-based classification of irAEs with specific incidence rates, grading criteria, and tiered management strategies, serving as a practical clinical reference.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Management recommendations are largely based on expert consensus and existing guidelines rather than novel randomized controlled trials presented in this paper.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4394b63dfe98f3127580588e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies and categorizes diverse risk factors, highlighting the role of gut microbiota and genetic polymorphisms, pointing towards precision medicine approaches.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Many identified risk factors (e.g., specific microbial strains, genetic variants) are noted as having 'promising' but 'not yet universally validated' predictive value; the paper acknowledges the lack of reliable clinical biomarkers.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe1b12ddfb220879142c6003\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI therapy (anti-CTLA-4, anti-PD-1/PD-L1)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Core mechanisms involve Treg exhaustion, Teff overactivation/cross-reactivity, B-cell autoantibody production, cytokine network imbalance, and monocyte/macrophage inflammatory cascades.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ead3e8fc0c45a6993b000063\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Risk factors analysis\",\n          \"finding\": \"Risk is influenced by host factors (age, sex, BMI, comorbidities), gut microbiota dysbiosis (e.g., Akkermansia muciniphila abundance), treatment regimen (combination therapy increases severity, dose-dependency), tumor type/histology (high TMB/high burden), and genetic factors (HLA polymorphisms like HLA-DR4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6798e317fab01f72ee02f0e6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Organ-specific irAEs\",\n          \"finding\": \"Different organs have distinct incidence and severity profiles; e.g., anti-CTLA-4 is linked to colitis/hypophysitis, while anti-PD-1/PD-L1 is linked to pneumonitis/thyroid dysfunction. Rare but fatal events include myocarditis and myasthenia gravis.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::913dc3cf94d1412f8a58d6ea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Correlation with efficacy\",\n          \"finding\": \"There is a partial statistical correlation between certain irAEs (e.g., vitiligo) and anti-tumor efficacy, suggesting shared antigenic targets, but excessive immunosuppression may diminish efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a675abe54cac9b7e7d6cc86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3080cc085a00ab0269bfdf5e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review addresses the critical challenge that while ICIs significantly improve cancer survival, they cause severe, multi-organ irAEs due to disrupted immune tolerance. Key problems include the lack of reliable predictive biomarkers, incomplete understanding of molecular pathophysiology (especially for rare/fatal irAEs), complex toxicity profiles from combination therapies, and the controversial correlation between irAEs and anti-tumor efficacy. The goal is to provide a systematic framework for clinicians to understand, predict, and manage these toxicities.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::862ed7699d67d89644832217\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) used in cancer therapy, specifically examining the mechanisms, risk factors, and clinical management of immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It covers various organ systems (skin, gastrointestinal, endocrine, cardiovascular, etc.) and discusses future research directions. The scope includes solid tumors generally, with specific mentions of melanoma, lung cancer, renal cell carcinoma, and hepatocellular carcinoma.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc846e4ef365893a676fab0b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This is a comprehensive review article published in 2025 that systematically summarizes the pathophysiology, risk stratification, and clinical management of irAEs associated with ICIs. It details how ICIs disrupt immune homeostasis through T-cell dysfunction, B-cell autoantibody production, cytokine dysregulation, and monocyte-mediated inflammation. The paper categorizes irAEs by organ system, providing incidence rates, grading criteria, and treatment guidelines. It also identifies multiple risk factors including host characteristics, gut microbiota, genetic polymorphisms, and treatment regimens. Finally, it outlines future strategies for prediction, prevention, and targeted intervention to balance anti-tumor efficacy with safety.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10c4da75004fc002b1e4e2e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The association is observational/correlational in the cited studies. The paper emphasizes the *dual effect*: these same microbes may also increase irAE risk. It does not provide mechanistic depth on *how* exactly the microbiome modulates efficacy beyond general immune activation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Mentions that high abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (>4.8%) is associated with prolonged overall survival in NSCLC patients receiving ICIs, attributing this to enhanced CD8+ T lymphocyte activation and IFN-γ secretion. Also notes that other microbes can enhance antitumor immunity.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::309fa2b34a73f9b249924c60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The mechanistic details provided are largely inferred from general immunology or cited animal/experimental studies. The paper explicitly states that the molecular interaction networks require further investigation. It does not detail specific microbial metabolites or precise signaling pathways linking microbiota directly to tumor antigen presentation or T-cell priming for efficacy.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Describes mechanisms where gut microbiota influence T-cell subsets (e.g., Th17 differentiation and function). Dysbiosis may disrupt Th17 homeostasis, leading to hyperfunction and pro-inflammatory cytokine release. It also mentions that specific probiotics/prebiotics can alleviate irAE symptoms, implying a regulatory role.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f8ea0c7f877777d642503dc8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of Akkermansia muciniphila having a 'dual effect' (enhancing survival but increasing irAE risk); mention of gut microbiota regulating Th17 cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9cd0d7630fcef01909adb663\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Statement that despite many potential biomarkers (including microbiota-related ones), there is currently no universally acknowledged reliable biomarker for predicting irAE risk.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d68a0a45b28262f047176315\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The paper's primary focus is on *adverse events* (irAEs), not efficacy. Any claims about efficacy modulation are secondary mentions or part of the discussion on shared mechanisms/toxicity risks.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::45538ddfc2fb94b27b1abfa3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The link between gut microbiota and efficacy is described as correlational (e.g., abundance levels associated with survival) rather than definitively causal or mechanistically fully elucidated in this text.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7fb4e1dd9b8b2e79cb3e9d81\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Specific microbial species mentioned (e.g., Akkermansia) are linked to outcomes in specific contexts (NSCLC), and results may not be generalizable to all solid tumors or all ICI types without further verification.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::56536e998c235c8881061947\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanisms involving gut microbiota are often summarized broadly (e.g., 'regulating T-cell subsets') without detailed molecular pathways, requiring caution when inferring specific causal chains.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::53339ce4b7ad243f4de96c8b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::dad3b7f35d836145e9d03851\",\n          \"snapshot::a28036d77e210b3d249c89e2\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e55a8c9d389564d56630951\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69b79394d0726b95b6065fa9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1788373d25e3a170db3bb0aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 队列设计：两项前瞻性非随机队列（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），基于疗效（PFI≥1年）和irAE严重程度（≥2级）将患者分为获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组。采用地标分析（Landmark analysis）以1年为界评估irAE，减少 immortal time bias。2. 多组学分析：宏基因组测序鉴定物种丰度、共现网络、功能通路（如SCFA合成基因）；代谢组GC-MS定量SCFA。3. 分子模拟分析：将微生物序列与自身免疫疾病抗原库及肺癌抗原/抗癌肽数据库比对，识别交叉反应表位。4. 菌株水平分析：使用StrainPhlAn分析大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌的SGBs变异及系统发育信号。5. 外部验证：在McCulloch（黑色素瘤ICI）、Routy（NSCLC ICI）等公共数据集上验证SCFA预测值和抗原模拟结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::27dd931bd58169567e4a4506\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"首次提供实证证据支持微生物组通过分子模拟驱动irAEs（自身免疫抗原模拟）和ICI疗效（肿瘤抗原模拟）的假设。揭示了长期获益者特有的紧凑微生物网络和丁酸高产能力。明确了菌株水平变异（而非仅物种丰度）对临床表型的决定性作用。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（宏基因组n=54，代谢组n=49），可能限制统计效力。抗原模拟分析依赖于公共数据库中的已知表位，可能遗漏未表征的关键表位。菌株分析仅针对丰度较高的少数物种。所有样本为基线采集，无法反映治疗过程中的动态变化。外部验证队列的治疗方案和肿瘤类型不完全一致（如黑色素瘤vs肺癌）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48c7437a9bc25839f3746846\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比获益组与耐药组（宏基因组预测+代谢组验证）\",\n          \"finding\": \"获益组富集丙酸（P=0.01）和丁酸/异丁酸（P=0.12/0.02）。乙酸、丙酸、丁酸水平越高，PFS越长，肿瘤进展风险越低（HR<1, P<0.05）。丁酸生产主要受乙酰辅酶A途径介导。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a4e6d4ef4b3160f0c43baaa5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比irAE组与非irAE组\",\n          \"finding\": \"irAE患者微生物中与系统性红斑狼疮（SLE）、皮肤/结缔组织自身免疫病相关的抗原表位对齐数量更多，特别是在免疫性结肠炎患者中SLE相关表位显著富集（P=0.04）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f2e549ea2a38a11164f7f0ca\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"对比高疗效组与低疗效组\",\n          \"finding\": \"高疗效组微生物中与肺癌相关的抗原和抗癌肽（ACP）表位对齐数量更多（P=0.07/0.06），并在Routy队列中得到部分验证（P=0.02）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7cfa37c4ed6bd29db16e931a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"特定物种（大肠杆菌、普拉梭菌）\",\n          \"finding\": \"菌株水平变异与临床表型强相关。例如，普拉梭菌SGB15342在获益组中富集，而SGB15323/332_group倾向出现在严重irAE组。不同组间存在高突变率，表明菌株特异性决定功能。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd986072923c2c8b143e0469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f1aa6ce49462b4fc36bf4e98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组影响ICI的初始疗效和irAEs，但其对长期生存获益的具体影响及底层机制（如代谢物、分子模拟、菌株变异）尚不清楚。特别是区分长期获益者与耐药者或仅发生irAE者的微生物特征差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8723f2c5d07d798f6a11ec0f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"中国北京协和医院晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，接受抗PD-1/PD-L1免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗。研究聚焦于基线肠道微生物组与代谢组特征对长期疗效（无进展生存期PFI≥1年）及免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）的影响。样本分为长期获益组、严重irAE组和耐药组，并通过外部公共队列（McCulloch, Routy等）进行验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6739f5f8fdd552af3ccd0592\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在阐明肠道微生物组如何影响肺癌患者ICI治疗的长期结局及其潜在机制。通过前瞻性收集基线粪便样本进行宏基因组和代谢组测序，结合临床随访数据，分析微生物组成、短链脂肪酸（SCFA）水平、分子模拟现象及菌株变异与临床表型的关系。研究发现，长期获益患者拥有更紧凑的微生物网络和高产丁酸/丙酸的能力；irAE患者的微生物中存在与自身免疫抗原相似的表位；响应患者的微生物中富含与肺癌抗原相似的表位；且特定物种（如大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌）的菌株水平变异与临床表型显著相关。这些发现为“智能”粪菌移植提供了理论依据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1853254a590326de7a98b136\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"数据主要来自肺癌患者，虽在黑色素瘤队列中验证了丙酸/丁酸趋势，但需注意肿瘤类型的异质性。关联性强，但因果链条需结合其他干预研究理解。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了SCFAs（乙酸、丙酸、丁酸）作为预测ICI长期疗效的生物标志物的实证数据。具体指出丁酸生产依赖乙酰辅酶A途径，且高水平SCFA与延长PFS和降低进展风险相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d439e44dd010530a60fd704\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"分子模拟的证据基于序列同源性比对，属于相关性/预测性证据，尚未通过体内实验直接证明T细胞交叉反应。抗原数据库可能存在偏差。菌株分析仅限于少数物种。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了并初步验证了“分子模拟”机制：1) 微生物抗原模拟宿主自身免疫抗原导致irAEs（特别是SLE相关表位在结肠炎患者中富集）；2) 微生物抗原模拟肿瘤抗原增强ICI疗效。同时强调了菌株特异性（如大肠杆菌毒力基因簇）在决定irAE或耐药中的作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f9084d13af5236dab61bb354\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Co-occurrence networks showing compactness in benefit group; enrichment of butyrate producers like F. prausnitzii, Blautia.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::12d03fe22e6c6021e4b4f5e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion section proposing 'smart' FMT based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdc428f23c1a35942c603cdd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的分子模拟结论是基于生物信息学预测（序列比对），并非直接的免疫学功能验证（如T细胞克隆追踪），在综述中应表述为“提示”或“初步证据”，而非确证机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a15aad3974479b8ec5c7e50f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"菌株水平的发现仅适用于大肠杆菌和普拉梭菌等丰度较高的物种，不能推广到所有微生物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d73df87bb79df88cf488a874\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"外部验证队列（McCulloch, Routy）在肿瘤类型和治疗方案上与主队列存在差异，解读时需考虑肿瘤微环境异质性的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d5f0d5e9220739bab7fe6fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"irAE分析采用了地标分析以校正时间偏倚，这是该方法学上的优势，但在比较不同研究时需注意终点定义的一致性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dba1ca498c98136c62e2487b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study employed landmark analysis to minimize immortal time bias in irAE assessment and validated efficacy-related metabolite findings in external cohorts (Routy, McCulloch). The discussion proposes a 'smart' fecal microbiota transplantation concept based on strain dynamics and antigen mimicry profiles. The study design was a non-randomized, unblinded, prospective cohort with median follow-up of 1167 days.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-u2gi65cq\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_4e312d3d88\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The specific request for large-scale microbiome association studies focused on non-colitis irAEs (such as myocarditis or neurotoxicity) is not fulfilled by this material. While this study includes some non-colitis irAE cases (e.g., cardiovascular, muscle) within a composite 'severe irAE' group, the total sample size (n=13 for severe irAE) is small, and there is no dedicated large-scale analysis for specific non-colitis subtypes. The authors' own admission of limited sample size confirms the ongoing evidence gap regarding statistical power for specific irAE subtypes.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated gut microbiome and metabolome associations with long-term ICI outcomes and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) in a prospective cohort of lung cancer patients (metagenome n=54, metabolome n=49). The authors grouped patients into benefit, severe irAE, and resistance categories. The severe irAE group (n=13 in metagenome cohort) included various irAE types such as cardiovascular toxicity (2 cases), muscle toxicity (1 case), endocrine, skin, and gastrointestinal toxicities, rather than focusing exclusively on colitis. Mechanistically, the authors reported that microbiota sequences from irAE patients aligned with autoimmune antigenic epitopes (molecular mimicry), particularly noting SLE-related epitopes enriched in colitis patients, and that beneficial outcomes correlated with higher short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) like butyrate and propionate. Strain-level variations in Escherichia coli and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii were also associated with clinical phenotypes. The authors explicitly stated in the limitations that the sample size was relatively small due to strict quality control and long-term follow-up requirements.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41eac1d693544443b3b7f8f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::51342908369a3d1c46566ac3\",\n          \"snapshot::59aab1e2a170fac4e9fc15c6\",\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a51e25fe21f9f078bc3908f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::0e9c11fd9439a46e9f2334bc\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::293eb3790a6ab7b71a0f7938\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ac4a925240c145b25c1cbb1a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b5fdca1762c4a1844c7341f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用混合研究设计：1. 临床观察性研究：前瞻性收集93份来自37名抗PD-1治疗肺癌患者的粪便样本，以及61份来自33名发生irAEs的多癌种患者样本。使用16S rDNA扩增子测序进行微生物组分析，计算α/β多样性，使用LEfSe识别差异菌属，并通过随机森林算法构建irAE预测模型。2. 动物因果验证：将C57BL/6小鼠经抗生素鸡尾酒处理清除原有菌群后，分别移植来自有结肠炎型irAE患者和无irAE患者的粪便菌群。随后给予抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4单抗诱导免疫反应，评估结肠炎发生率、疾病活动指数、组织病理学及炎症因子表达。3. 功能机制推测：基于16S数据使用Tax4fun和KEGG数据库预测微生物功能通路，重点关注短链脂肪酸（如丁酸）产生菌丰度及代谢途径差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::56a251bb4bf2e70d9046ac70\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了在非黑色素瘤实体瘤（主要是肺癌）背景下，肠道微生物群与irAEs发生的关联证据；区分了结肠炎型与非结肠炎型irAEs的微生物特征差异；通过人源化小鼠FMT实验提供了微生物群导致免疫性结肠炎的因果证据；识别出丁酸产生菌丰度降低可能与irAEs发生有关。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（最终纳入分析的无irAE组34人，irAE组32人），可能导致统计效力不足或过拟合风险；仅使用16S rDNA测序进行功能预测，缺乏宏基因组或代谢组学的直接验证；基线前ICI治疗前的粪便样本获取困难，限制了基线状态的全面分析；无法完全排除irAEs本身对微生物群的扰动影响（尽管FMT支持因果方向）；预测模型需外部独立队列验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::370e1997ec04811460303373\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1治疗后出现irAEs的患者 vs 未出现irAEs的患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物组成显著不同（P=0.001）。irAE患者中双歧杆菌（Bifidobacterium）、粪杆菌属（Faecalibacterium）和阿加索细菌属（Agathobacter）丰度较低，而红球菌属（Erysipelatoclostridium）丰度较高。主要丁酸产生菌总丰度在irAE患者中更低（P=0.007）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f62b887d1b251fb36e63bda9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"结肠炎型irAE患者 vs 非结肠炎型irAE患者\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物组成显著不同（P=0.003）。结肠炎型患者中拟杆菌属（Bacteroides）和双歧杆菌丰度较低，肠球菌属（Enterococcus）丰度较高。主要丁酸产生菌丰度也较低（P=0.018）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5d30a37ab62a73ee8b4c7454\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"小鼠FMT实验（结肠炎型irAE供体 vs 无irAE供体）+ 抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"结肠炎型irAE-FMT组小鼠中3/9发展为致命性严重结肠炎，而非irAE-FMT组0/9发病。结肠炎小鼠表现为体重下降更快、DAI评分更高、结肠缩短、组织损伤更重，且结肠组织中Il6和Tnf mRNA水平升高。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10c3dff98fb8682a1dccf79f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"irAE预测模型构建\",\n          \"finding\": \"基于10个主要差异菌属（以Gemella, Dubosiella, Atopobium为主）的随机森林模型在训练集AUC为86.4%，测试集AUC为91.7%。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3ae97f7b7005bd50f7ba304f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::684b173aec03df76f4198b59\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物群影响ICI疗效，但其作为irAEs发生和严重程度的角色及其因果关系尚未确立。特别是针对除黑色素瘤以外的其他癌症类型（如肺癌），以及不同器官受累的irAEs，微生物群的差异特征和作用机制尚不明确。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5f0274b3487f40b29fe60c92\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为接受抗PD-1治疗的晚期胸廓恶性肿瘤（主要为肺癌）患者，以及发生免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）的多种实体瘤患者。研究情境包括临床队列观察和基于人类粪便微生物移植（FMT）的小鼠实验。范围涵盖不同严重程度和器官类型的irAEs，重点聚焦于结肠炎型irAEs。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f157d433e5f5ba636b80c1ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物群与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗引发的免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的关联及因果关系。研究首先通过16S rDNA测序分析了接受抗PD-1治疗的肺癌患者及发生irAEs的其他癌症患者的粪便样本，比较了有无irAEs、不同严重程度（1-2级 vs 3-4级）以及不同部位（结肠炎型 vs 非结肠炎型）患者间的微生物组成差异，并构建了预测模型。随后，通过抗生素预处理小鼠并进行来自不同患者组的FMT，结合抗PD-1/CTLA-4抗体治疗，验证微生物群对免疫性结肠炎的因果作用。最后，利用功能预测分析探讨了潜在的代谢机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d89e4d7c6b3d84ae3a62e9b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"样本局限于晚期胸廓肿瘤和多癌种irAE患者，结果可能不适用于所有ICI药物（如抗CTLA-4单药）或早期癌症人群。预测模型未经外部验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群组成与ICI治疗安全性（irAEs发生）的直接关联数据。具体显示irAE患者中特定有益菌（双歧杆菌、粪杆菌、阿加索细菌）减少，有害菌（红球菌属）增加。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::65232b9dd11887f7c3c947ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"小鼠模型使用了抗生素预处理和联合抗体治疗，与人体的生理状态存在差异。功能分析仅为基于16S的预测，非直接代谢物测量。并非所有接受FMT的小鼠都发病，表明其他宿主因素也参与。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"通过FMT小鼠实验证明了来自irAE患者的微生物群能够因果性地诱导免疫性结肠炎。同时指出丁酸产生菌丰度降低和特定代谢通路（如氨基酸、维生素代谢）的差异，提示代谢机制可能在介导irAEs中起作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::57b8483e9f9cd672d266dba2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文引言部分回顾了微生物群在ICI疗效中的作用，并指出目前研究多集中于黑色素瘤，强调本研究扩展至肺癌等其他实体瘤的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::97d2a1c8337589808f154b48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"论文讨论了Faecalibacterium在不同研究中的矛盾结果（有的报道保护，有的报道促炎），并归因于情境依赖性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a0a5e2ac2060afd26a3d218\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的因果证据仅限于小鼠模型中的结肠炎表型，不能直接外推至人体所有irAEs的发生机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f23786cce1eeced11074defa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"预测模型的AUC值基于内部验证，可能存在过拟合，实际临床应用价值需进一步确认。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::821df0a3c6305c95bb399a78\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"功能预测基于16S数据，准确性低于宏基因组测序，代谢通路的差异仅为推测，需代谢组学验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::68071cd7d3b466b520eab039\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量较小，特别是严重irAEs亚组分析可能缺乏统计效力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43b7ecec9c980646e0f0b9dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有研究（包括本研究）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少（如本研究仅 3 例心肌炎）而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，无法充分验证或解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题。\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0ae65bd0a736c1c537cf2b1c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"研究建立了 irAE 预测模型（训练集 AUC 86.4%，测试集 91.7%），但该模型针对的是广义 irAE 发生，未针对特定器官毒性进行验证。小鼠 FMT 实验证实了来自结肠炎 irAE 患者的微生物群可因果性诱导小鼠免疫性结肠炎，但未涉及非结肠炎表型的因果验证。功能预测显示丁酸产生菌在 irAE 患者中丰度降低，提示代谢机制可能参与，但这基于 16S 预测而非直接代谢组测量。\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"Ch6_gap_5\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\chapters\\\\external\\\\N4452dfb25f491e9335fe-5a6b848383c152a3\\\\round_1\\\\supplements\\\\Ch6_gap_5\\\\attempt-fc662a0y\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_cef6ae84bc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"目前仍缺乏针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎、神经毒性）的大规模微生物组关联研究。现有研究（包括本研究）通常将非结肠炎 irAEs 合并分析，或因特定类型病例数过少（如本研究仅 3 例心肌炎）而无法得出具有统计效力的结论，无法充分验证或解决 P0051 和 P0530 中提到的证据不足问题。\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"该研究纳入了 32 名发生 irAEs 的患者进行微生物组分析，其中非结肠炎 irAEs 被归为一组进行分析。在具体 irAE 类型分布中，38 例 irAE 事件包含 3 例心肌炎（myocarditis），但未对心肌炎或神经毒性等特定非结肠炎类型进行独立的微生物组关联分析。作者在讨论部分明确指出，由于样本量相对较小且 irAE 发生率总体较低，亚组分析（如比较不同类型 irAE 患者的微生物组）可能缺乏统计效力或无法进行（'subgroup analyses may have lacked statistical power or were not possible, for instance for comparing the microbiota of patients with different types of irAE'）。该研究证实了结肠炎与非结肠炎 irAEs 之间的微生物组存在整体差异，但未能提供针对特定非结肠炎 irAEs（如心肌炎）的大规模独立数据。\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41536b078798585a9f6cf46f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0600\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::764ddb58c7d47204119c72b5\",\n          \"snapshot::715592e26e584e7d4af212b0\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"source_identities\": {\n      \"P0096\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0096\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0096\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"The Gut Microbiome from a Biomarker to a Novel Therapeutic Strategy for Immunotherapy Response in Patients with Lung Cancer\",\n        \"doi\": \"10.3390/curroncol30110681\",\n        \"paper_id\": \"261e0a3618ae7acf6e831646379929eff88857d5\"\n      },\n      \"P0146\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0146\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0146\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"Gut microbiota shapes cancer immunotherapy responses\",\n        \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41522-025-00786-8\",\n        \"paper_id\": \"4171288ecca93c6bca3eee61295418d704bb00fd\"\n      },\n      \"P0585\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0585\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"Gut Microbiota in Advanced Non-small-cell Lung Cancer Receiving Chemo-immunotherapy: An Ancillary Biomarker Study from the Phase III trial JCOG2007 (NIPPON).\",\n        \"doi\": \"10.1016/j.jtho.2025.02.026\",\n        \"paper_id\": \"8016df1aa5a8160b7ccd412fa6851a6a508e2731\"\n      },\n      \"P0298\": {\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0298\",\n        \"source_id\": \"source::P0298\",\n        \"aliases\": [],\n        \"title\": \"Gut microbial signatures and immunotherapy outcomes in NSCLC and melanoma: a 